@keys[�"Breaking News!"lI'm live here at <imp>Tri Island</imp>, a mysterious island discovered recently off the coast of Makya."�Trainers from all over the world are making their way over as there have been sightings of extremely rare Pokemon and resources."�With no region claiming major jurisdiction over the island, there have been reports of multiple factions creating base camps in the area."}The only thing that's certain here is the battling as Trainers duke it out over territory and access to these new wild areas."NBut for now, we'll be providing live coverage of the event. Over and out."1Uh -- yes? Did you want to ask me something?"LWell then don't -- can you not -- I'm not a big fan of being stared at."�I just like... I’m a wanderer. Or, rather, not a wanderer -- but I don't have a home -- or, well -- excuse me. I spend most of my time in caves."�I don't know? I mean -- no, I know, but rather I'm not sure why -- I mean, what kind of question is that? I'm a Pokémon trainer."AOr I was. And I’m... rather good at it. And not much else."bA friend's. Just a friend's. I'm good at -- they entrust me with the training. I get results."aI mean, that sounds -- that's not what I really meant. I'm -- I'm -- I was -- let's move on."(Heyo, \PN. Hear you’ve been busy."YYou’re just racking up badges like they’re nothing, huh? Mavis must be so proud."5It’s not a compliment. Just stating the facts."~And the fact is that you’re not getting anywhere now unless you come meet me, for reasons that make me too angry to explain."*I’ve got a <imp>gift</imp> for you."�I’m literally friends with two - I mean ONE - of those gym leaders, and I was the commanding officer for half the people keeping track of Rafael."Word gets around."kI also know that you’re gonna have some issues getting <imp>across that river</imp> without my help."Yikes."Yeah, Mavis is… Mavis."CYou know, you… ah, nevermind. Eye on the prize and all that."JSpeaking of which, you need to get <imp>across the river</imp>, yeah?"0We might be able to reach an arrangement...")But. But... you know how this works."TQuid pro quo, yeah? I know you’ve scratched a few avatars off of my hit list."TGonna be clear as crystal here: you’re doing better than most of the rangers."gSuch as the ones that recently just got mauled by a particularly ornery <imp>Titanix avatar</imp>."SYou know me so well. Put the thing in the ground – well, more in the ground."cIt’s ripping through the mine yard in <imp>Grouz</imp> at the moment, which is… a problem."YIf it goes down particular routes we could be facing a VERY uncomfortable situation."IThe rangers? Dealing with rampaging Tauros and crossroads hauntings."gAvatars are out of their paygrade. Not that we don’t send them in anyways and hope for the best."hSpeaking of which: <imp>Grouz</imp>. Squad went out and didn’t leave a scratch on the damn thing."/You can split it right open, though, yeah?"YYou don’t know what busy looks like, kid. You think I’m not trying to work here?"fI know you cut a deal with Helena. Same here: you accelerate my timetable, I do the same for you."USo make your way down to <imp>Grouz</imp> and turn that Titanix to slag. Please?"rI’ll check back in on you when I hear that behemoth’s gone. Promise I’ll make it worth your while, too."Capisce? Good. Bye."…She hung up."ABefore you can put your phone away, it starts ringing again."%It seems like an important call."*\PN, I need your help. It’s urgent."4You know the <imp>catacombs</imp> under Prizca?"JThere’s an entrance in the <imp>sewers</imp>. I need you here, now."ZI’ll explain when you get here – this isn’t the most secure way to communicate."DIt’s bad, though. Real bad. I need a trainer of your caliber."[Thanks. I know this is sudden, but I can’t overstate how much I need your help ASAP."JListen, kid, if I could call in a couple Chasm strike teams, I would."uBut things change, and now all I have is you. You are NOT going to like the consequences if you don’t help me."Please."=Bring the best team you’ve got. It’s gonna get ugly."?Hey, just checking in. What’s going on? Making progress?"SOh, wow. Really trying your li’l heart out, aren’t you? More than one gym!",Ah, don’t get all broken up about it."[You could be in the big city with six badges under your belt and it wouldn’t matter."Why, I never."6Haven’t you heard blood’s thicker than water?""Practically a type advantage.")Well, whatever -- keep your secrets."8As for me, I’m taking a break before facing Noel."nYou don’t know him -- and, let’s be honest, you probably never will -- but he’s kind of a big deal."bSo while you’re scuttling to and fro like a Falinks without an officer, I’ll be relaxing."Wish you were here!"He hung up…"(Wow, that was… a complete breeze."A joke, honestly."&That’s my sixth badge now. You?"Wow. I remember that."1Wait, how did you even schedule a challenge?"4I made an appointment before I got on the ship."2You... you're serious about this, aren't you?"That can’t be right."You’re better than that."UNot by much, but if you’re lying, then… you’re taking this seriously. Huh."Hah! That never gets old."LYou remind me of… I guess a Zangoose, right? So angry, but so normal.",But you are really angry, aren’t you?"\Well, you’ve certainly made good time, but this is where things start getting harder."1You’ve still got a lot of ground to cover."!See you at the championship!"4I’ll make sure to look in the stands for you."He hung up… again."/Hey, \PN. Things going well on your front?"0Good. You’ve got eight badges now, right?"xThat’s... it’s something. You’ll excuse me if I’m not too preoccupied with the whole gym challenge shebang."That makes one of us."KBetween the avatars and... recent developments... I’ve been swamped."XYeah, frickin’ tell me about it. I know exactly what you’re talking about, too."ZListen: I know the stress is probably getting to you, but we’re in the endgame now."_Be a hero, become Champion, go home to Mavis. Everyone’s happy, right? Smiles all round."(So, yeah, just a li’l bit longer."}Take down those avatars if you can spare the time, come back to Prizca for the Championship, and... we’ll see about Yezera."&Thanks, \PN. I know it’s a lot."Thanks."MWhoever the hell it is helping Yezera, they’ve been making the rounds."iGood news is that you seem to be their priority. Haven’t been, y’know, rampaging. Which is good."�I’ve had zero luck trying to track them down. I’d hire Alessa again if she’d return my calls – but, hey, that’s why I have you, right?"Yes and no. You’re gonna have to cut through some of the best trainers in the region, but it ain’t just busywork this time."jNot that it ever is – thanks, by the way – but this one should be especially interesting for you."jThat’s what I like to hear. This ain’t gonna be an easy operation, but I trust in your abilities."gMostly in committing violence. Lots of violence. Though, actually, maybe try talking this one out?"4You’re gonna want to hear this one. Trust me."wI mean, you’ve got a minute before the Championship anyways. This op is... it’s pretty dire, importance- wise."gI’ve got a confirmed sighting on Yezera. She’s back in her hometown – <imp>Whitebloom</imp>."eYezera’s got a few titans on her and some kind of master plan, so she’s your first priority."a\PN... thanks in advance. Try and be understanding with Yezera. She’s... dealt with a lot." But do what you have to do."\Do what you have to do, come back to Prizca for the tournament, and go home a Champion."$Happy endings all-round, right?"Right. Bye."2Apologies for the interruption, young master."%Or should I say, young champion.""My heartfelt congratulations."...""Regardless, I bear good news."VYou have received a formal invitation from MonumentSoft, a subsidiary of LuxTech."AThey desire your presence at the <imp>Battle Monument</imp>."hApparently it hosts quite the grueling challenge, an “AI Trainer Gauntlet” as they describe it."EThere is to be some manner of reward for successful completions."eT