riment!"Sorry about the tricks."?It's really hard to repeat this one, but I'll try my best."1Swadloon is looking lovingly at its trainer."2The area up ahead is the battle testing site."WIt's where LuxTech scientists observe the capabilities of Pokemon in test battles."ZIt is recommended that you don't participate until you have at least four gym badges."eHowever, if you make it to the end, we do have a reward for you--some tech that no one else has."UParticipate in battles against our scientists, and you may earn a hi-tech prize."|Do be careful though, if you're not yet at the right skill level. Four badges is the threshold our data suggests is optimal."AYou look skilled enough to participate. Please, go on ahead!"ZLooks like you prevailed against our most skilled staff in this facility. Great work!"7Truly, nothing fires my neurons quite like coding."sIt is for this reason that I embarked on my quest--to construct the perfect artificially intelligent trainers!"#I beg you, please battle them!"lThere's no reward to earn by defeating them, and your Pokemon will learn nothing from the experience..."MBut you and I both, well, we'll gain terabytes of wisdom about battling."4Need I remind you--knowledge is its own reward."|If you're worried about difficulty, note that the battlers automatically adjust their levels to match your skill level."[I am sure you will learn a lot from the experience of battling my Artificial Trainers."DIn fact, I'm betting on these being an excellent training tool."*My government contract depends on it."uIf my project succeeds, it'll be implemented in some tourist attraction they're building off the southern coast."_My dad brings me to work every day after school since I like to watch the Pokemon battles."VYou get to see all sorts of Pokemon here. Sometimes the Trainers let me pet them!",Pokemon defense mechanisms are amazing!" Time to see them in action!"+You pierced right through my defenses!"/Is there ever such a thing as enough data?";Begin 