ht here if you decide you want to experience this marvel of science yourself!"aHm? Be sure to check how much money you have before you answer in the affirmative like that."LOne of my colleagues studies Galarian Fossils over at the ol' Chasm HQ."�She's the only person in the region that can revive 'em. Lotta genetic junk in there that requires some weird knowledge to figure out."4I wouldn't know much about it, I study ecology."&"Aerodactyl, Terror of the Skies""[Specimens of Aerodactyl's evolved form, Pteroflyte, were only found recently in Makya.".Oh? Tyrantrum has something in its mouth."ATyrantrum has a big smile for you! Its teeth are very large!"XEverybody knows about the small white totems that are common throughout the region."wThe archeological consensus was that they were religious artifacts from an ancient race that worshipped Regigigas."AAfter years of studying them, we moved on to other subjects."9But then the totems suddenly started <i>glowing</i>!"LNobody has been able to figure out how that happened, or what it means.""Scattered Shells""�Omanyte have no bones, except the modified bones that form their shells. Therefore only the shells were left behind to become fossils.""Dueling Rampardos"":Rampardos' skull withstands impacts of any magnitude."<As a result, their brains never get the chance to grow."iThe new expansion to Star Dungeons 2 just dropped, so I don't care about anything you'd have to say."8Unless you have a peculiar fossil you want revived."...and $2000..."*That would be worthy of my attention.""Then leave me to my grinding."?Wow, you have very little money. That's almost impressive.")Like a low percent run of real life.",One second, one second... 3% HP left..."=Yes! Nailed it. Best dungeon clear time in all of Makya."Oh, it's you! Thanks to the samples you gave me earlier, I've become the best-in-slot expert on these new ancient Pokemon."GSure, they're not exactly "historically accurate", but who cares!?"DMy favorite games come to life... an army of mobs, loyal to me!"Muahahahaha! Ahem."jSeeing as it wouldn't have been possible without you, I'd be happy to... split the drops, as it were."]If you want one of these new species, tell me. But not if I’m in the middle of a raid!"2Ah, my accomplice. You're here for a Pokemon?"LMonthly subscriptions aren't cheap, so I do need to ask for some money."!Just $5000 should be enough."LOr if you have another whole fossil, I can revive it for you for $2000."Which one were you after?"\PN hands over $5000.""Here you go, freshly spawned."'There's more where that came from."#You don't have enough money..."HSorry. I know you're a noob, but even my generosity has its limits." Thanks for wasting my time.""Kabuto Eternal""~An ancient Pokemon with a niche as a seafloor scavenger. Living examples are still rarely found to this day in the deep ocean.""The Noble Aurorus""gThis fossil was found perfectly preserved in the Svait Ice Cave, astounding Team Chasm scientists."5A dazzlingly complex video game is being played."iA giant, many-limbed monster is being attacked by a group of people with wildly mismatching outfits.""Simple Plant Life""tFar from the advanced trees and bushes of today, ancient plants had a simple structure of single leafed blades."No"Yes"M. Kabuto"M. Omanyte"Revive Fossil"Never mind[H"#"Armaldo, Amphibious Predator""kIt lived on land and went out into the sea to hunt for prey. Its sharp claws were its greatest weapon."8A 3D scan of a Pokemon bone is displayed on screen."MIndividual chambers of the marrow can be seen in detailed cross-section.""Nascent Life""�In ancient times as in now, eggs are the favored way of Pokemon to deliver their offspring. Eggs appear in the fossil record of every era."fI'm an expert at fossil ressurection. For a low fee of $3000 I can revive any fossil you give me!"/Would you like to have me revive a fossil?"dYou'll find me right here if you decide you want to experience this marvel of science yourself!"aHm? Be s