 salad, leftover pasta, and a glass of milk."<You take some silverware from Helena's kitchen cabinet."pYou eat a third of the salad before switching to the pasta. It tastes surprisingly good despite being cold."%You chug down the glass of milk."4A lonely, third-eaten salad lies in the fridge."-You can't. You've already taken so much.",You pull yourself away from the fridge."GYou take the last of the silverware from Helena's kitchen cabinet."JLooks like Helena will need to do the dishes whenever she comes home."=You slowly consume the remaining salad. It's acceptable."The fridge is empty."7There's nothing left, you've completely raided it."8You notice some cutlery in the overhanging cabinet."UIf you wanted to, you could probably use it carve someone's name onto the table."(You carve your name onto the table."0You carve the name "Yezera" onto the table."2You carve the name "Tamarind" onto the table."(…Oh. So you’re the other guest."!I guess it could be worse…"It’s – I mean, yeah."?If – if it could be anyone, you’re… I’ll take you."Yeah. I’m sorry."9I shouldn’t’ve – I shouldn’t’ve come here."EI shouldn’t’ve answered the phone… why did I even pick up?"$Well… I do have another team."AThey’ve given me another one to train, and you’ve grown."?I – I mean, you have to have gotten better. I need to…"*sigh* Sorry. Nevermind."2Tamarind wanted me here. She wanted you here."TShe hasn’t shown up yet. I… I only really know one way to kill time. Ready?"Oh. OK."0I can – I guess we have to wait, anyways."<Thanks. I’ll try not to – I won’t disappoint you."This I can do."Hah. Maybe I – no."I can’t."=I would, but I need to train these Pokémon. I promised."fBut, if you want to face Artemisia and Autochthon and the rest… I promise you will. Eventually."0For now I’ll keep using these. You ready?"*She always runs late, right… right?"8Does she just not want to… oh! Are you ready now?"	Hah!"That was good.",I’m – oh. I’m sorry, I’m… no."9You’re… you’re like a Pokémon, you know that?"IBut also like – you’re like me. I think. Maybe I’m projecting.""Oh? Well, thank you. I think."OIt’s easy to talk to you, but you can talk back. You’re a real person."KAnd you’re a trainer – a great trainer! I want to ask you so much."EYou’re – you can talk to your Pokémon. You understand them."]I mean, I don’t speak their language but – I’m sorry, I can’t explain very well."EI only speak well… I only speak dueling. And you speak it too."Oh."�I guess that’s – I mean, that’s my life. First the arm, and then the shyness, and then suddenly you’re a thirteen-year-old hero and – oh. I’m so, so sorry."QI go on tangents. Especially with you, it seems. I’m… it’s mortifying.")…Yeah. I would too, if I were you."FIf you could be anything, I wouldn’t… I wouldn’t choose me."3The world must be really nice for you. To you.">I don’t – I can’t blame you for hoping I’m wrong."FYou two got acquainted, then? Damn. Nary a scratch on this place."xHonestly, I bring the two most explosive duelists I can find to Helena’s house and you can’t even break a vase?")My luck… well, you’re both here."J\PN, meet Yezera, former Champion. Yezera, meet \PN, future Champion."_I wanted you two to meet, but I’m kinda getting the feeling you already know each other."MFigures. You’re an explorer, and she keeps away from the beaten paths."#Or any paths at all, honestly."@Oh? Then things really have changed since last time we met."0For both of you, now that I think about it."Now that’s just grand."vWhat I wanted, honestly. I’ve basically been shipping you two – except, y’know, with violence instead of…"0I should’ve left that thought in my head."Anyways…"<Hah! So you’ve gotten the same treatment that we did."DShe’s good at what she does… and bad at what she doesn’t.")Yezera… I can’t just ignore you." Even if you’d like me to."+Are you OK? I haven’t seen you in…"+Over a year. Two since we’ve talked."?I’m – I’m fine but – I can’t. I can’t do this."*Not with both of you – I’m sorry."/Well… at least she’s alive and intact."IYezera. The girl that took down Team Chasm. First Champion of Makya.":Mystery disappearance, manhunt, no tracks, the works.";She’s grown since then… but still a nervous wreck."1Anyways. You didn’t come here for history."I wouldn’t go that far."6It’s stupid, is what it was. The whole shebang."But, yeah, anyways. Gift."-Yeah, I’ve wasted enough of your time."3That gift I mentioned – let’s get to that."VIndeed! I wanted to get you to meet her, but I know your type. I can bait a hook."�Well, if you’re interested I can – actually, it’s probably better for you to hear it from her mouth. You’ll see her again."2She wouldn’t let a potential challenger go."	But!"Your gift."ZSince avatars turned the bridge to flotsam – and, yes, I TOLD THEM to reinforce it!"bThey didn’t, since they trust ex-Chasm about as far as they can throw them and – anyways!"ZFor very stupid, avoidable reasons, the river’s basically uncrossable without Surf."kIf you’re like me, you’re not gonna pack a Water-type everywhere you go, so just use this instead."]It’s just more practical. Stylish, too! Assuming you’re good at it. Which I’m not."&Go have fun and get those badges."lOh, and, uh, this is Helena’s place, so feel free to eat some of her food or something before you go."�Kick a vase over. Carve your name in the table. Er – maybe someone else’s name. Yezera’s name! She’d get a kick out of that. Heh."-You see your name carved onto the table."5You see the name "Yezera" carved onto the table."7You see the name "Tamarind" carved onto the table."=A vase filled with flowers sits delicately on the floor.":You could totally smash this thing, if you wanted to."*You decide against smashing the vase."fYou find a garbage bag, put the flowers in it, and swing it against the wall with all your might."RA garbage bag filled with rubble is all that remains of this once proud vase."Don't take the food."Take the food."Don't carve."Carve your name."Carve Yezera's name."Carve Tamarind's name."Good 