very different."I hope I'm not."We've met."We're friends."We're rivals."Unfortunately."It's interesting."Get to the point."You had a gift?"Actually, I kinda did."Don't smash."Smash.Iu;␀Y[[�"2I've been stationed here to look for avatars.">I haven't been able to find any, though, so let's battle!"HI can probably take a break, with Trainers like you walking around."See ya."<Well, they don't pay me to bring my Max Revives home...")I'm tending to my Pokemon right now.""A portent felt, a divination."Chaos freed, eradication."Wishes are a solemn curse."&Left to rot, and they will burst."%A chain of flowers holding fast."#Will it crumble? Will it last?"+Old times renewed, ones you must face."+In lashing out, they find their grace."(YEEHAW, ALL ABOARD THE LOG EXPRESS!"=RECKON TO FACE US ON MORTAL, HEARTPOUNDING, LOG COMBAT?!",WOWIE! That was some fine log battling!":Any log rider is a friend o' mine, don'chu forget it!"jWe're just making sure that the logs sent downstream by the local Bibarel don't clog up the waterway."?It's honest work, and we get to have a little fun with it."RGood battle, Trainer. I'm sure everyone on the Stretch enjoyed watching that."	Hey."Gettin'... kinda nervous."/Tamarind’s gonna show. I’m sure of it."�Told her to meet me inside. I’ll go around the back, you go in the front, we’ll cut her off, no problems, clean and easy. Capisce?""Great. Like, yeah, of course."You’re my friend, right?"=Oh, yeah, I’m, like, yeah. I’m, like, totally ready."See? Normal Candy!"GDon’t be silly. We’re, like, totally gonna make things better."At least a little bit.";Um, like, good question, but isn’t it kinda obvious?"hLike, she’s gotta confess and tell us what she did, right? And then we’ll bring her to justice!"Y...OK, to be, like, totally honest with you: I’m worried you’re gonna betray me."SBecause she, like, did you a favor and you’re working with her and all that."vBut you won’t. I mean, like, she caused all of this! This entire place is mega-screwed because of what she did!",Eh! No! No talking! I can’t hear you!"}I am one hundred percent not interested in, like, anything you’re saying. I trust you. I trust you, and that’s that."lSo you go in and I’ll scoot ‘round the back, and we’ll do a pincer maneuver, alright? Let’s go!"West: Eleig River Crossing"East: Canal Desert"UI've been managing the wildlife here for years, I've become an honorary Bibarel!"aWhoa! That last move almost smashed the whole dam! I'll get right back to work fixing it up!"aAnother day, another trainer recklessly battled on this new dam. My Pokemon love the thrill!"?This is such a nice spot, I should bring a couch out here."kUsed to look a little more pretty before the Biberal cut down the trees, but I appreciate the company."Um... hey."9So, Tamarind and I, like, kissed and made up? Kinda?"GUm, not in that way. She’s like twenty-five years older than me."@I... \PN, I still really hate her. She is, like, the worst."�She’s this snooty arrogant brat that literally destroys things that get in her way for no reason. But, like, I can’t just punch her and make it better."...But I did punch her."ENot really! It was kind of a wimpy punch. Still, I had to do it."For baby Candy, at least."#I know, I know! It was stupid."VBut, like, I’ve thought about it so many times, and now I finally got to do it."LIt didn’t make me happy, but I can scratch it off the list, y’know?"DOh, not even. She deserves to be punched, like, at least twice."6What? That punching her doesn’t make it better?"hOr that I, like, decked her in the first place? Because the answer is yeah, I’m a learning Candy."HReally, I let her off easy. But, um, I didn’t really let her off."sI kinda... got hired? Like, I do not trust that hag for a second, so I’m gonna stick to her like a Remoraid."OShe’s gonna fix all the messed-up stuff that she and her cronies caused."OAnd she’s, like, totally overworked, so, um... yeah. I’m her aide now!"#And bodyguard. And conscience."WI get to get 