 elsewhere, rumble."AYou listen more closely, but there is nothing more. Silence.".Samorn? Don’t worry about that bastard."DC’mon, let’s get you out of here. We can take care of this."iGo deal with the issue – you’re the better duelist. He’s down in the lower area causing havoc."BYou take care of that, I’ll help Samorn. Move it, Slowpoke."@These ruins are old, but not as old as the mountain itself."\Whoever they were, they must have dug extensive tunnels with pre-industrial technology."REither that, or something powerful created an entire mountain on top of them."Oh, it’s you."0As you might’ve heard, you’re too late."Again."XOur tasks are complete, and now we play the waiting game. But I’m… not patient."aLook at these statues – monuments to monuments! Idiocy! They’re begging to be destroyed."HShh. If you won’t be a placid audience, you’ll be escorted out."Testaments of an age."0Delicate as ever. Fine. Cease bothering me."]What’s the point of resisting, or creating? We’re going to pave it all over anyways."oAnd I don’t mean that philosophically. I will replace all of this with malleable white stone personally."A blank slate."VUnlike Yezera, my perfect world is one in which human whim gets what it deserves."OSpeaking of which, you’ve yet to be crushed underfoot. Let’s fix that."F…Well there goes Registeel. Hard to keep a hold of, those ones."4What can I say? I’m… only human, after all."NFine. It can rust away in its tomb for all I care. It’s irrelevant now."I'm out of here."$An item was left on the ground!"	Hey."6I, uh, heard everything when you fought that guy."LYeah, yeah. Just scraped up a little. Nothing a Heal Pulse can’t fix."<Can’t tell if you’re being a sarcastic snot or not."/Doesn’t really matter. You’re welcome."/Hey, listen, this’ll only take a minute."CI just wanted to tell you… hell, is that really how I sound?":Like that edgelord? Just another self-absorbed prick?"8Heh. You’re squirrellier than a Furret sometimes."-Ah, you don’t have to tell me. I know."No sugarcoating it, huh?"Yeah. That’s fair."KYou’re being polite even now? Or are you actually telling the truth?"dListen, it really hurt admitting that you’re better than me back there. As a trainer, I mean."rBut somebody had to fight and somebody had to get Samorn out, and I’m a lot of things but I’m not stupid."XYou’ve always been better. I knew it, Mom knew it, and you… I hope you know it.">This entire competition was stupid. Mom knew you’d win."OThis was just a scheme so she could finally prove you’re better than me."…Yeah."$You know Mavis as well as I do."]I mean, yeah, makes sense. She wants an heir to the company… to the legacy… you fit."OYou know it is. Mavis is just as cutthroat as Helena – hell, maybe more."YYou think a normal mom would encourage her kids to have a showdown a continent away?"	Hah!"(It’s just that easy for you, huh?"]You’re right, of course. Just took me a lot more mulling it over to get to that point."_I’m calling this whole thing off. It’s stupid and I’m not playing that game anymore."^I’m going to collect my badges, do my best in the Championship, and then I’m leaving."PYou can tell Mavis whatever you want. She’ll offer you a job at her side."5Take it or leave it, your choice. But I’m out."%Thanks. Gonna need it, honestly."Yeah. Sure as anything."Ha. Maybe, yeah."`But I’d rather be called a yellow-bellied spoilt rich kid than Mavis’s second-favorite."MGonna be honest: don’t really care. Like I said, you do what you want."xBut, yeah, I’ve been thinking about this for a while, and that whole debacle back there with Samorn… I’m out."RI’m not gonna do the whole edgy trainer pushing as hard as possible shtick."CI do really hate you sometimes, but that’s siblings for you."5Had a Hymnus to try out against you, too. Shame."c…Bye, \PN. I’ll see you around. Good luck… saving the world, or whatever you’re doing."?Samorn’s Flygon is flitting anxiously, stirring up dust."ZWheewie, this whole Regigigas thing-y going on here is a whole kerf