Yeah."No."That's not true."Then stop it."Good luck."You sure?"Coward."I'm with you.;[g"LLeaving through -- oh. You -- you’re looking for something down here."2Come back and, uh, I’ll still be... around."<Down the stairs, \PN. See red or whatever it is you do."..."IThe statue is motionless, yet you feel something, elsewhere, rumble."AYou listen more closely, but there is nothing more. Silence.".Samorn? Don’t worry about that bastard."DC’mon, let’s get you out of here. We can take care of this."iGo deal with the issue – you’re the better duelist. He’s down in the lower area causing havoc."BYou take care of that, I’ll help Samorn. Move it, Slowpoke."@These ruins are old, but not as old as the mountain itself."\Whoever they were, they must have dug extensive tunnels with pre-industrial technology."REither that, or something powerful created an entire mountain on top of them."Oh, it’s you."0As you might’ve heard, you’re too late."Again."XOur tasks are complete, and now we play the waiting game. But I’m… not patient."aLook at these statues – monuments to monuments! Idiocy! They’re begging to be destroyed."HShh. If you won’t be a placid audience, you’ll be escorted out."Testaments of an age."0Delicate as ever. Fine. Cease bothering me."]What’s the point of resisting, or creating? We’re going to pave it all over anyways."oAnd I don’t mean that philosophically. I will replace all of this with malleable white stone personally."A blank slate."VUnlike Yezera, my perfect world is one in which human whim gets what it deserves."OSpeaking of which, you’ve yet to be crushed underfoot. Let’s fix that."F…Well there goes Registeel. Hard to keep a hold of, those ones."4What can I say? I’m… only human, after all."NFine. It can rust away in its tomb for all I care. It’s irrelevant now."I'm out of here."$An item was left on the ground!"	Hey."6I, uh, heard everything when you fought that guy."LYeah, yeah. Just scraped up a little. Nothing a Heal Pulse can’t fix."<Can’t tell i