g you off easy. Sorry. Beating folks into the dirt is my job, after all."CAh, well. Guess no matter how hard I try, old habits die hard."BSpeaking of dying hard – lay down and quit moving, will ya?"PHah. They ain’t never been happy with my way of goin’ about covert ops."BToo rough ‘nd tumble. I ain’t built for cloak-and-dagger."iSo, let me tell you straight: you listen to Yezera. You hear her out. And don’t you dare hurt her."KAll I ask. And, uh, I wasn’t just sent here to chit-chat. You ready?"1Hey. Fancy meeting you in a place like this."aOh, don’t look so angry – Regirock and I are here to fight you, but we’ll get to that."RI know you’re more than a pretty face. You’re smart. Care to hear me out?"0Aww. I knew I had a good feeling about you."[How do I explain it… well, I hate to use the word, but modern society is degenerate."_We’re distant from the perfect moment of creation. We’ve kind of taken over the world."UNo respect for our elders – the primordial Pokémon that created the universe."zYezera’s going to reset this world back to its origins. And then humanity will be in the bosom of Arceus once more."kDon’t call me insane. Although I’m sure this arrogant, faithless civilization would use that term."QI’m merely devout, and devotion means making sacrifices. For example: you."EI really do like you, but… we all have to sacrifice sometimes."MGodlike Pokémon are now treated as not much more than beasts of burden."MAvatars are destroyed at will because they’re “threats to humans.”"\The world has lost all respect, the divine essence from creation diluted and destroyed."NAnd since you seem to be no different, I can take some joy in this fight."�Arceus created the world. It is pure, and perfect, and resetting the world back to its original form will let us be pure and perfect too."BI’d like to see myself blessed by the grace of our creator.")I’d like to see you that way, too."In time."CFor now, I’ve been ordered to slow you down. Shall we dance?")Good. I knew I saw something in you."BSome spark of faith. I’m a… very good judge of character."�I’d love to just talk with you for a while, but I was explicitly instructed to stop you. So we’ll fight. Don’t take it personally."Oh. Was I too forward?"HMy emotions tend to get the better of me. I’m almost heartbroken."%Well, I suppose I am a stranger."uFortunately, I’ve been sent to slow you down, so I have a convenient vent for all these feelings of rejection."Hello, friend."FBusiness before pleasure: I have been sent to slow your progress.".To that end, I am accompanied by a titan."XBefore we attend to that, however, may I interest you in a short, frank discussion?"RI would rather like to try to convince you of the legitimacy of our position."Thank you for your time."_Yezera’s goal is to recreate the conditions of the world shortly following its creation."oModern science has attained almost complete understanding and mastery over the world – the modern world."�It cannot, however, understand the past. By reverting existence, we may study the universe from its conception and obtain universal knowledge."#This is the only way to do so."vWithout the reversion, humanity will never attain complete understanding of the universe. It is worth all prices."RNow our time for conversation is up, however. Regirock, please do the honors."AAll persons who attempt to advance civilization should care."HUniversal knowledge is a prerequisite for an all- powerful society."\That is my goal. That is the goal of all science: to know, and to apply that knowledge."\Your ignorance implies discussion will get us nowhere. Let us dispense with such, then."<Knowledge will be retained into the new primordial era."8We can rebuild at least small enclaves of humanity."\From there our analysis and conquest will begin: a new society with absolute knowledge."@And, stemming from this absolute knowledge, absolute power."YConsider it. In the mean time, there is the business I mentioned earlier. Excuse me."|I am glad you have the wisdom to agree. If you should wish to support us in our endeavors, I will be happy to have you."xWe will fight for a more enlightened era. For now, however, I must slow you. Business is business. Let us commence."II find this highly unfortunate. You will be left behind by progress."NIf you would prefer to retain your ignorance, however, I cannot help you.".Prepare yourself. Regirock, if you would."Oh. Hey."IYeah, so, I knew you’d be here. Gym challenger, and, uh, all that."…Welp. This is awkward.";How do I say this… you interested in hearing us out?"bWe’ve kinda got the upper hand, but, y’know, don’t really wanna fight you. Whaddya say?"=Oh. That’s good. Great. Honestly didn’t expect that."HWell, I just figure we’ve done a lot of ordering Pokémon around.">Maybe it’s time to even up the footing a bit, y’know?"8We can all kinda make up for whatever we did wrong."mThe others have their reasons, but, uh, this is mine. Make a world where we can be forgiven. You get it?"(Well – fine. You know what? Fine."dI don’t need your permission, and we certainly don’t need your help. Regirock. Do ‘em in."Z…You so sure? Takes a lot of pushing to train a team that strong in so little time."4But, yeah, no, I get it. Why would you help us?"?Rich brat. Maybe we can beat some responsibility into you."NUh. Don’t really know how to break it to you. You… don’t have time."EFor one, we’ve already just about won. For two – think fast!"*Regirock, sweep ‘em off their feet!"*Oh. Didn’t, uh, really expect that.":Figured you were kind of a stuck-up brat. No offense."=Well, good. Maybe we’ll be side by side one day, yeah?"5But, uh, for now… I’m supposed to fight you."HSo, uh, sorry – ah, what am I saying, we live for this. Ready up."Yeah, I guess that tracks."#Fine. That’s… it’s fine."5I came here to beat the crap out of you anyways."kOdds are Regirock isn’t gonna stick around much longer, so let’s make it count. Try your best, eh?"…Hey."xTsk tsk tsk. I’m not gonna lie to you: I’ve been trying to plan this conversation in my head for the past hour."RBut, um, you kinda interrupted me. So can I just say what I want to tell you?"BWelp. Listen, uh, Makya’s kinda in a weird place right now."]Team Chasm ran roughshod over this whole region and then kinda just… got away with it?"So, uh, yeah, if you ever wanted proof that humans can’t get even the most black-and-white justice right, there you are."KWould’ve been simple to fix that little screw-up. But they didn’t."[So we’re taking the power away from humans, and putting it in the hands of Pokémon."Is it? Is it!"AAm I insane for wanting some damn PUNISHMENT in this world?!"DWell, guess what. If people won’t give me it, I’ll MAKE it.""And I’ve got just the tool!"%It is simple, you – you idiot!"aI can track down every ex-Chasm criminal and haul them up to the courts myself if I have to!"UThey just won’t do anything if I did! So I have to do things personally, yeah?" Sorry. Nothing… personal."	Yes!"MThey’re noble and pure and – and – and they’d never let me down!"/Unlike you! And everyone else around here!"JYou want to see? C’mon. See what kind of justice Pokémon can give!"Oh. Ah-hah."LKinda got myself a bit worked up there… welp, no harm, no foul, yeah?"…Nah, that’s stupid."^I’m not gonna waste this chance. I’ve got a Regi. You’re a prodigy. Let’s RUMBLE!"Urgh, you make me so mad!")Nobody will frickin’ listen to me!"
Fine."Y’know, fine, whatever."?You get what everyone else I fight gets. What you deserve."?Regirock – your watch is over. If you would go, then go."YSo it returns to its resting place… no matter. It has done all I desired and more."%As for you, we shall meet again."YFarewell, and do not pursue me. Fate and fate alone will dictate when we next speak."eRegirock’s damn well spent. Flighty li'l things never like to be outside their tombs too long."*Ah, well. Got what I came for anyhow."�Let me tell you one last word of advice. You hurt Yez, I’ll find you. And it won’t just be for some play fight with animals."jG’evening, kid. I’ll see ya around. Make sure I don’t hafta hurt you too bad when I do, ‘kay?";Au revoir, Regirock. Enjoy your entombment, I suppose."PAnd as for you, that was an exciting fight. You’ve got my heart pounding."yIf you want to join us, come find Yezera. And if not, well, we’ll meet again. I’m looking forward to it already."So long."4I surmise Regirock will now return to its tomb."gThe titans are temperamental and ill-suited to existence outside their crypts. It is of no matter."AWe have all but succeeded in our plans. This was a courtesy."7I will take my leave now. Thank you for your time."/There it goes. Back to where it came from."_Well, didn’t really expect to win anyways. Just wanted to slow you down, and, uh, I did.":So… bye. We’ll do this again sometime. I’m out."P*sigh* Buh-bye, Regirock. We don’t really, uh, need you anymore, I guess."?It was fun while it lasted… welp. Nothing lasts forever."ISpeaking of! Hopefully next time we talk it’ll be in a fair world!"KIf it isn’t, then, uh, I’ll give you a run for your money, ‘kay?"\Toodles. And don’t you dare follow – I’m playing hard to get, so respect it. Hah!"uMore than a million years ago, a meteor struck this area of Makya, plowing through a large mountain to the west."XThat large mountain became two smaller mountains, which we now know as Split Peaks."NThe impact site itself would fill with water and become Sweetrock Harbor."0The ocean to the east brings calming winds."KBut why? We might explain it with ocean currents, or weather patterns."FBut what makes the winds here calming? Of that, I am not so sure."<I really want to know who that was in the weird outfit.";Well, regardless, thanks for kicking them out of town."=I'm a firefighter, so I'm used to dealing with issues..."DBut "Cultist with a Regirock" is outside of my job description."Lightkeeper's House"Artisan Orbs" Sweetrock Elementary School"/"In loving memory of Mrs. and Mr. Diakos.""HI've been biking across the entire region over the past few months.":Crossing the Split Peaks was by far the hardest part."nThe view from these cliffs, and the feeling that I've finally accomplished my goal, made it all worth it."West: Split Peaks"South: Sandstone Estuary";"Sweetrock Harbor, satisfying the world's sweettooth!""!"A sister city of Canalave!"":I work at Sweetrock Candy factory, like many in town."IThat said, I rarely get to see Victoire, the manager and gym leader.":I gotta rely on rumors to know what her team is like.",Some of them are a bit hard to believe."DI heard some people saying that she uses a Sticky Web strategy."AWith Fairy and Steel-type Pokemon? How does she manage that?"$Huh, you really beat her, then?"4You gotta tell me what she's like as a trainer.""My curiosity's grown too big!"_Sweetrock Candy is sent all over the world, but more than 30% ends up in the Galar Region."#Those people love their candy."+Shh... don't give away my hiding spot!")Is it... is it safe to come out now?")How goes your journey, young master?"YI've purchased a Clefable teleportation license, and reserved this pier for our use.":We can travel to and from any of our usual locations."Where will we be heading?""Emma's Empoloreum!""0An Empoleon standee points you to the door."+Have you slid down the conveyor belts?"=Preeeetty sure we're not allowed to, but it's crazy fun."PMaybe not as fun as beating the 7th gym will be with my snazzy new Pokemon!";Which ones? You'll just have to battle me to find out!"XI cannot convey to you just how much I want to battle. Heh. So, you up to doing so?"Understood."+I'll be here until you wish to battle."Rock 'Em, Torterra!"9Damn, even these 'mons couldn't leave a dent in you."EThink anyone in the lighthouse was watching our battle just now?"INo way around it, I'll need some healing before we square off again.",Got a good look at Victoire, I take it?"bShe as quirky as they say? I don't know why I bother asking. I'll be finding out soon myself."0The 7th badge... oh so sweet will it taste!"Sweetrock Harbor Gym"Leader: Victoire"The Candy Queen!"Sweetrock Candy Outlet"kWhat was once a printed notice has been covered entirely by a poster advertising the EXP-EZ Dispenser."Sweetrock Lighthouse"#Today's a good day for gaming."-A Piplup standee points you to the door."Berry Greenhouse"HI love to slide down the conveyor belt. But, my dad doesn't let me."UI have to stay by the school until he gets off work so I don't get into trouble."I'm gaming over here!"No."	Yes."I’ll listen."Don't need it."No, I don't."That's tenuous."I'll think about it."
I do."Fine, talk."Not interested in talking."I know who you are."Don't threaten me."Clear."Wish that already."I'm with you."Alright, fine."Go away."That's insane."Degenerate?"Arceus's bosom?"That's fair."Sure, talk."Don't really care."It isn't worth it."Who cares?"Society will crumble."Good point."I'll listen."Don't care."You're wrong."I'm not guilty."
Sure."Not that simple."Pokémon would do better?"Fair enough."Maybe later."Sure, let's go.Iu;␀�%[[O"=A cap of rock is holding back a geyser of boiling water."PI was once considered a beauty, but the way of the water needed a disciple."I should dry off."_Legends say if I stay here for fourty day and nights, my inner qi will strengthen tenfold."4The way of the water is full of solice. Splash."W\PN! You made it. Took some effort to find this place but... man. It was worth it."7What? My all-grown-up companion here? Yeah. It is."\Sorry. Well, not sorry. You didn’t have to come. But you did. And I’m glad you did."dI think it’s soothing. I dunno, maybe I’m just a little more goth than I’d like to admit."|The waters here are special. Not just ice-cold and way too deep for me to be comfortable, but they’re saltwater, too."cOcean water, trapped down here. And for some reason... it makes Phione transform into Manaphy."CI don’t know why, or how. I’m not that smart. But it does."�I don’t even know if it’s really evolution. It’s – I don’t care. I don’t care how it works, or what it is scientifically."6It’s a Manaphy now. And I’m damn proud of it."(Yeah! I mean, I think so, at least."YI can’t believe it. A Pokémon of actual literal myth and legends, here beside me."Oh. Uh, yeah, thanks."�Um. I didn’t really have a lot to do with it. Phione came down here, danced around in the water here, and then it just kinda... transformed."KUnbelievable. A Manaphy. I raised a Pokémon like this, all by myself."oIt’s a Pokémon from myth. Supposedly they live at the ocean floor and can befriend anything and anyone."iThey’re not half-bad in a scrap, either. Truly just... amazing. An absolutely incredible Pokémon."vAnd it’s my best friend. It doesn’t hate me, or resent me, or fear me. It chose to be with me, of all people."mIt could’ve chosen anyone. It could’ve chosen you – you’re certainly a better trainer than I am."lAnd, yeah, thank you, sincerely, for everything. You’re great. And you’ve really helped me. Thanks.";Hmm. Yeah, not good enough. Gonna need one last favor."qI hope so! Not too many people have even seen one of these magical things. And fewer people have fought one."@Oh, we’re on the same wavelength. You know what it means."CThat’s right. One last showdown. You and me. My new Manaphy."QI’m gonna lose, I know. But I’m not going down easy, alright? You ready?"4Alright. Get ready. I want it to be a good one."<I’ve never been happier to throw down against anyone."oManaphy’s debut. I don’t care if it’s good or bad. I just want to see it in action. Let’s do this."(You good? I’m ready when you are."*Ah, wouldn’t have it any other way."IYou know, \PN, you’re a good friend. You don’t pull any punches."GI never could beat you, and I’m never going to, but that’s OK."WYou’ve made me better. Helped me out. I hope I’ve helped you too. I really do.")And, uh, yeah, I’m glad I met you."rGood. I’m – yeah, that’s all I’ve ever really wanted. Manaphy’s happy, you’re happy, I’m happy."FSorry, that’s just who I am. Big ol’ bleeding-heart, I guess."Oh!";Uh, well... I don’t know. I’ll think about it, OK?"NWe’ll see each other around. I, uh... I dunno if I see you in that way."?You know. If you’re saying what I think you’re saying."D...\PN, I really do care about you, though. You’re my friend."1And if you need me, I’ll be there, always."^Well, maybe not always. I’ve got my Pokémon to take care of. But you know what I mean."/I’ve done some stuff I’m not proud of."ZI’m gonna come clean: I’ve been working with Yezera on her plans for a while now."�Never felt like I was good enough. Didn’t feel like anyone was good enough for the love we got from our Pokémon. But maybe that was just me projecting."�Maybe I’m the asshole, y’know? And I’ve known that forever – I’m not that stupid – but it takes a wake-up call to realize it. And this was it."�So, yeah, if they want to ruin the world, they can do it without me. And you can stop them with a Phione at your side. Or a Manaphy now, I guess."II’ll be thinking about you. Wishing you the best, now and forever."IThanks for all of it. If you need me, ever, all you gotta do is ask.",Neither of us is finished, I know that."JI’m gonna try again at becoming Champion next year, I think. Maybe."GFuture’s uncertain. And you... you’ve got stuff to do, I know."DI wish you the best. I’m gonna be thinking about you, I know."cAnd if you need me, you damn well better ask me, OK? You’ve taken a weight off my shoulders."See you around, \PN."Is that...?"Tell me about it."Creepy, isn't it?"That's great."I'm proud of you."What's a Manaphy?"You're welcome."It was worth it."You know what this means."Not yet."Let's rock."Same here."Don't get sappy."Coffee sometime?[O"=A cap of rock is holding back a geyser of boiling water."PI was once considered a beauty, but the way of the water needed a disciple."I should dry off."_Legends say if I stay here for fourty day and nights, my inner qi will strengthen tenfold."4The way of the water is full of solice. Splash."W\PN! You made it. Took some effort to find this place but... man. It was worth it."7What? My all-grown-up companion here? Yeah. It is."\Sorry. Well, not sorry. You didn’t have to come. But you did. And I’m glad you did."dI think it’s soothing. I dunno, maybe I’m just a little more goth than I’d like to admit."|The waters here are special. Not just ice-cold and way too deep for me to be comfortable, but they’re saltwater, too."cOcean water, trapped down here. And for some reason... it makes Phione transform into Manaphy."CI don’t know why, or how. I’m not that smart. But it does."�I don’t even know if it’s really evolution. It’s – I don’t care. I don’t care how it works, or what it is scientifically."6It’s a Manaphy now. And I’m damn proud of it."(Yeah! I mean, I think so, at least."YI can’t believe it. A Pokémon of actual literal myth and legends, here beside me."Oh. Uh, yeah, thanks."�Um. I didn’t really have a lot to do with it. 