ll fold to you, though."Well, you got me."HLook at you, phasing through the walls. Who are you, Danny Phantom?000Iu;␀�[["/Being back at the Fin is pretty nostalgic."{Feels like just yesterday I arrived here in that rusty fishing boat, ready to take on the world as part of Team Chasm.",And we did! Take on the world, that is."8Not really in the way my younger self had intended."0Have you been to the Starter Store in Novo?"QIt's the only place to get your hands on those highly coveted starter 'mons."JProblem is that they require a token exchange instead of just cash..."gWish I had one of those instead of the Normal-types that fraud of a professor likes to give out...["9Estar de volta à Nadadeira é bastante nostálgico."�Parece até que foi ontem que cheguei aqui naquele barquinho de pesca caindo aos pedaços, pronta para conquistar o mundo como parte da Equipe Chasm."6E foi isso que fizemos! Conquistar o mundo, digo."IMas não exatamente da maneira como minha "eu" mais jovem imaginava."2Você já esteve na Loja De Iniciais em Nova?"[É o único lugar onde você pode conseguir os altamente cobiçados Pokémon iniciais."SO problema é: eles exigem uma troca de fichas ao invés de apenas dinheiro..."jQueria ter um daqueles em vez dos tipos Normal que aquela professora de araque gosta de distribuir...;["/Being back at the Fin is pretty nostalgic."{Feels like just yesterday I arrived here in that rusty fishing boat, ready to take on the world as part of Team Chasm.",And we did! Take on the world, that is."8Not really in the way my younger self had intended."0Have you been to the Starter Store in Novo?"QIt's the only place to get your hands on those highly coveted starter 'mons."JProblem is that they require a token exchange instead of just cash..."gWish I had one of those instead of the Normal-types that fraud of a professor likes to give out...Iu;␀N7[[{"OThis is a pickaxe! It was used to dig a tunnel underneath the Split Peaks.":That tunnel took over <imp>6 years</imp> to complete."fWhenever saccharite was discovered, digging would be paused until the mineral could be extracted."+Mining saccharite takes time and care!"T<imp>Question for Kids</imp>: Have you ever been underground? What was it like?"Yo, champ in the making!"QSamorn might not look like it, but she was one of Team Chasm's top battlers.".Her specialties are Dragon and Bug-types."gThat makes Ice-type your silver bullet. She'll have some answers for it, but it's still a counter."qFlying and Rock are your next best bets. Steel is pretty good as well, since it resists both of her typings."7Best of luck in the final stretch of your Gym run."-Hoho! It's rare to see Samorn so lively."-Watching you two go at it was inspiring."The PC is turned off."\With how quiet the gym is, you think it'd stand out as rude if you tried to turn it on."4This statuette is made of a special white clay."RStatuettes like this, commonly known as "totems", are found throughout Makya."OThey are protected by regional law. Totems must stay where they are found!"nAnthropologists believe the spots where totems are found were of special importance to an ancient people."O<imp>Question for Kids</imp>: Why do you think these statuettes were made?"8Among the books on history, a scrapbook stands out."&The title is "Memories of Hoenn.""<A cute sticker of a Trapinch dominates the front cover."Sorry, am I in your way?")Wait, of course I am, I'm a trainer!";I've been reading about ancient Makyan hero- trainers."*You might be even stronger than them!"3I've got to stay here and continue my studies."An Eevee plushy."3A tag around its neck identifies it as "Lark"."+Beakers of chemicals line the shelves."*The majority appear to be weak acids."/The inscription is worn and hard to parse."KAh, \PN! I won’t waste your time by offering something hot to drink."4You’ve got a fight on your mind, don’t you?"8Good evening. Can I get you something? Tea? Coffee?"GYou’ve almost certainly wasted enough time here already, though."3Do you get nervous before facing a gym leader?"\I do – get nervous before facing a challenger, that is. I don’t want to disappoint."LI guess I shouldn’t worry. I’m called the Dreadnaught for a reason."PAre you in less of a rush than I thought? If so, feel free to stick around."I should’ve known."uExcuse me if I seem a bit terse. I’ll have to focus for this one. You’re not to be underestimated, you know."…Neither am I."BOf course. Now, if you’ll excuse me, I have to concentrate."…Let’s begin."J“Wrack and ruin broke our ships/And plucked us from our heavens.”"UOh, my apologies! It takes a short while to get my bearings again after a fight."eI get the same way when translating – which I have to assume is why that couplet came to mind.">Let me give you your badge. You’ve more than earned it."UWe don’t have to discuss it – I won’t infantilize you with obvious praise."\Speaking of plucking from heavens, though… you ought to know what that victory means."#Shall we chat a little longer?"&…Hmph. So you… ah, nevermind."[Ignore the ramblings of my battle-jumbled brain. It’s always a pleasure to duel you."…Huh. How clever."3You won, and I have a badge to present to you."[Goodbye. …Oh, excuse me. It takes me a moment to remember my manners after a battle."LCongratulations on your victory. I’d be happy to rematch you any day."TI’ve spent most of my career carefully breaking into sealed crypts and safes."=Years ago, though, I was also hired to help create them."�The wondrous abilities of the Regis made making nigh-impenetrable doors a cinch… but I’ve broken into a lot of impenetrable doors."=There is an avatar in a cave, high above where we stand."GI’d like to entrust this key to you, so that you can destroy it.".The past belongs in the past – forever."1Hello, \PN. Any good news about that avatar?"hNo? Well, then, I’m afraid I’ll have to withhold your tea and coffee privileges until there is."	Hah!"4Sorry, but I have to have some bargaining chip."!Go destroy that avatar, now."=It hides in a cave above our heads, on the mountainside."9Ah. So it’s done. I just wish we could’ve… no."(History is history. Today is today."OAnd tomorrow is tomorrow – a tomorrow without avatars, if we’re lucky."�Thank you, \PN. I think I’ll take a short break. You’re the last challenger I expected to see before the championship anyways."8You’re always welcome to stop by my home, though!"Two rusty iron longswords.",This is a ceramic statuette of a human!"EThe Ruins Digsite, nearby Team Chasm HQ, contains many of these."8They are estimated to be <imp>3000 years old</imp>!"uThey surround statues of the <imp>legendary golems</imp>: Regice, Regirock, Registeel, Regidrago, and Regieleki!"c<imp>Question for Kids</imp>: If you made a statue of a person or Pokemon, who would you pick?";I have to protect these relics from ruffians like you!"They belong in a museum!"(Must have misjudged your character."7Unlike me, you'd never steal a priceless artifact."
Tata!",I'll be keeping my one good eye on you."4A trash can made of some sort of tropical wood."It's totally empty."7A copy of a plaque found underneath Prizca Castle."dDated to around 1200 years old, the inscription is in an old Makyan dialect, and translates as:"/"The First Emperor reigns in these halls.""&"The faithful continue to serve."","A soul of fire cannot be snuffed out.""L<imp>Question for Kids</imp>: What do you think this inscription means?"4You'll have to get through me to fight grandma!"?Guess I'll go bother the scientists at the dig site again."DYou might have beaten me, but grandma's a lot stronger than me."=You must be pretty strong if you're challenging grandma."fNotes on the chalkboard describe a timeline of the Makyan monarchy, starting from 2800 years ago."<-- Archeology Hall"Classroom -->"wDated to around 1200 years ago, these iron swords were found in a large burial site discovered in southern Prizca."xBack then, that spot would have been next to the Eleig River, which was further north in the past than it is today."�Archeologists believe the site was the location of a large battle between the Kingdom of Prizca and an invading force from the east."x<imp>Question for Kids</imp>: Which things do you want to leave behind for the archeologists of the future to find?"ZThis blue rock is <imp>saccharite</imp>, an important mineral found throughout Makya."8Sweetrock Harbor is where most saccharite is found!"LSweetrock Harbor was created by an ancient <imp>meteorite impact</imp>."=Geologists estimate the meteor was about 67% saccharite!"J<imp>Question for Kids</imp>: How do you think that meteorite tasted?",Basic archeology techniques are listed."GThey're given in order of most to least destructive and dangerous.";The bookshelf is full of books on science and history.".They seem targeted at a younger audience."On second thought…"Let’s do this.[{"OThis is a pickaxe! It was used to dig a tunnel underneath the Split Peaks.":That tunnel took over <i