d probably learn to perform those moves.;["0A locked door. It has a slot for a keycard."'You insert the Team Chasm ID Card."#The door unlocks with a click."It's a vending machine!",However, it no longer holds any drinks."6A logbook with details on Avatar experimentation."GThe data on Primeval and Empowered moves is particularly thorough."NUsing this, a unique Pokemon could probably learn to perform those moves.0Iu;␀�a[[�"Are you ready?";You arrive even here undeterred… but not unforeseen."uYou have heeded Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, keepin' a lady waitin' like that."5Hah! Ain’t talkin' 'bout myself – meant Yez."qDon'tcha gimme that smile. She’s right fine when she’s dolled up, and more than that, she’s my friend."5You’re gonna give her your respect, y'hear me?"xNow, got some bad news for ya: I ain’t lettin' you have your last dance with her if I can help it. This ends now."OGlad to hear ya hearin' me. Now, kid, I ain’t 'bout to pull any punches."L'Cause you’re sweet and oh-so-polite, I ain’t gonna break anything."}But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid."6Ah, you’re such a babyface. Real cute one, too."nKinda kid you take home to meet your parents, y’know? Shame I’m gonna have to put you six feet under.">Hah! I kid, I kid – I ain’t doin’ wetwork. Anymore."OI ain’t lettin’ you get away without a few bruises, though. Ready? Go!"LHey – listen, she’s – don’tcha try goin’ and flusterin’ me."gHad to haul that girl to prom, mind ya, and she wears a nice dress a mite better than yours truly."XMy point is that’s she’s a right fine lady, and ya better respect her like one."IAgh, ya got me distracted. Quit with the psyops and fight me proper."WHah! Whatever you say, kid. I ain’t 'bout to take that metaphor and run with it."\You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliche but that’s my line about it."?I guess ya could say I’m reserving the first dance. Hah!"AI like you, kid. C’mere. Lemme beat that humor out of you."�Hello there. You arrived just a teensy bit earlier than I expected – I was writing a poem, see. Never to be finished, tragically."�These black arches of stone like a starless sky will soon be replaced by brilliant alabaster, which, well, ruins the central symbolism."GWhat a shame. I assume you’re going to force me to duel you now?"UYou march into my demesne, hauling your well- trained combat creatures with you."�We’ve fought before. You’re completely opposed to my beautiful dream. And you still want to claim I have a choice in the matter?"aDon’t insult me. You’ve made your choice, and now we have to deal with the consequences."]Ah, well. At least you’re honest. I like that about you. You’ve got such... clarity."�What a gleaming light in this dreary cave. Why, that could almost be poetic! If only we had a hopeless romantic to write that down."QAlas, I’ll be too busy directing my passions into carving your team apart."\Of course! You’re such a brilliant spark in this region. You deserve odes... sonnets."�On the other hand, the fact that you’re here now against me instead of alongside me means that you’re not as special as I thought."MNo faith. It’s a shame, really! I don’t want to do this! But I will."4And, since I have to... might as well enjoy it."JWhat? You think a poetic soul is creepy? Does true faith disturb you?"MGenuine emotions uncompromised by the endless drudgery of society? Fine!"UEnjoy where that narrow-minded view gets you. Namely: here, about to lose to me."Hello, friend."DWe have already begun. Regigigas will quickly remake the world."[I understand that you are here to face Yezera, but unfortunately I can’t allow that."�There is a non-zero chance of your success, and I am not a gambler. If you would like, we can both stay here and talk until the reversion overtakes us."FI supposed as much. Excuse me, but in that case I must fight you."gUniversal knowledge is approaching. I would like to be there to witness it – alone, if possible."cI do not either. Unfortunately, I can tell from your tone that we are, in fact, about to duel."zI am unwilling to let you go further, and I am unwilling to lose. Please understand... and please consider conceding."QThat is the most I am willing to say pertaining to your odds against Yezera."�She is conventionally regarded as unbeatable when she applies herself, though I am aware that you have broken that convention repeatedly."INow, may we end the discussion of theory and add another data point?"OExcuse my verbosity. If you would like to go straight to our duel, we can."gI would not insult your intelligence by pretending we will not fight. That much should be evident."Shall we?"=Oh, uh, hey. Listen: I’m gonna cut right to the chase."2You beat me once. You beat Yezera, um, a lot."mThough, some of those don’t really count, 'cause she was using someone else’s team and – whatever."`Point is, I can’t beat you. But… I gotta try. I’ve got a lot to answer for, y’know?"\Lotta little things I did that I got to make up for. Can’t you just let me have this?"BOf course you can’t. Can’t let me have anything, can you?"bUgh, I was gonna be Champion! I was really gunning for it, too. And then... yeah. Everything."dYou completely overshadow me in every way. I can’t beat you. But I’m gonna try to hurt you."bMaybe to you. But not to them – not to Pokémon. They’re the ones who have to forgive me."~It’s time for them to stop taking orders and start being treated like equals. That includes from ace trainers like you."_I know you can’t stand that, so... I guess we gotta fight. Sorry... but I’m not sorry."-I don’t. Not most of the time anyways."jI’m trying my best to make things right. Can you say the same? Going around keeping the status quo?"hIs this the world you want? I guess you’re a rich brat, so... yeah. Life’s easy, life’s good."IHmph. I’m gonna try and make it a little harder for you, if I can."+Sorry. Guess I’m a spiteful bastard."xNo! I’ll fail – I’ll gladly fail – but I’m not about to give up. I’ve got friends that need protecting."cI’ve got stuff in my past I need to make up for. And I’ve got a world that needs building."A better one – one that’s more equal, more fair. Sorry it isn’t what you want, but I won’t just roll over for you."You ready?"%...Hey. So, uh, this is it, huh?"]You’re, like, not gonna have a change of mind? No justice? No fairness? No punishment?"~Oh, who am I kidding – you’re Tamarind’s lapdog. You’ve been doing her dirty work since, like, literally day one!"8Guess what that means! That’s right: time to pay!"zThat’s what they all said. You’re not a team grunt! You’re just, like, a temporarily inconvenienced mastermind!"dUgh, you’re all the same. Well, I’ve chewed through a lotta grunts. No different this time!"'Nope! But I really really want to!"zTamarind’s out of my reach, but you’re, like, the second-best thing. So c’mere so I can give you a bloody nose."7If you were sorry you’d stop fighting me, idiot!"�You’re such a – such a dolt! How can I get it through your thick skull that you’re the bad guy? Can I beat it into you? Wanna find out?"�Oh, I swear, I’ll roll up these sleeves and deck you myself if I have to! I swear, if you chip my nails I’m gonna kill you for real!"=C’mon, boys and girls! We’ve got a beatdown to give!"Ah. Hah. Hahaha!"}So be it! My reading is complete – the scars of this battle left in the ancient stone here are a portent of things to come."TCan you suppose what it says? It says I shall lose here, and you shall triumph.".Hah! Fate has a sense of humor, it seems."`Go on. Continue yet deeper. I know my place, and will not stand against destiny any longer."qFor my sanity, I will refrain from attempting to divine the results of your future battles. I take my leave."%Awww, kid, you shouldn’t have."xGoin’ all-out? On yours truly? I’m touched. Not even half-honest, either – it’s a treat seein’ you fight."~Go on. Yez is waitin’ for you. I ain’t too hung up on this whole scheme. Yez’ll turn out fine either way – tough girl."RTougher than me, I swear. So you go do what ya got planned, whatever that is."WIf ya hurt her, they’ll never find the body, blah blah blah, you know the drill."AGood luck, kid. Come find me some time afterwards, y’hear?"0...Go. Leave. Now, before I lose my temper."dIs that really what the fate of the universe hangs on? Our relative skill in training Pokémon?"fIt’s ridiculous! It’s idiotic! I can’t believe – go! Just go! I should... I should... go."~Noted. Excuse me – I fear I may not have provided adequate resistance. I now find myself lacking any means to challenge you."m...Understood. I have no recourse but to retreat. I wish you the worst of luck in your future endeavors."KIf you will permit me to leave, I will no longer impede your progress."4Goodbye, friend. I hope never to see you again."Damn it. Damn it!"UI – yeah, that’s how it goes. Never was as good as you. Any of you hotshots."gPushed my Pokémon hard to try and get there, and now look at me. Trying to make up for all of it.":Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Manaphy. I guess that was it."VLet’s get y’all back to a Pokécenter, OK? Get you fixed up... I’m sorry..."AUgh! I’m – fine! Ow. I think I took a stray shot... oof."�Look me in the damn eyes, you dumb grunt! If I was – ow – if I wasn’t... if I wasn’t... I’m feeling a little lightheaded."RIs this why they black out after losing...? I’m gonna... I can’t do this."fGo do whatever it is you think you’re, like, actually accomplishing. You stupid, stupid dolt..."{But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put 'em up, kid."]You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliché but that’s my line about it."9Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Phione. I guess that was it.")I should’ve known she was useless."jYezera was THIS close. So close to getting everything she wanted. All she had to do was not tell you."}She had to not be human. Her one redeeming quality: her inhumanity. And now she went and betrayed that, and with it, me."0Apparently. It’s sickening, to be honest."tThe same shallow, stupid desires as everyone else. I guess I’m just as much of an idiot for believing in her."Yes. Good. For. Her."fUnfortunately, it isn’t so good for her grand plan, nor mine. I hope the catharsis is worth it."5Yes, she did. I’m glad you’ve realized that."(Fine. I hope I never see you again."HBut, well, I’ll take care of her once the regression is complete.";You, on the other hand, I’ll deal with now. So long."XDo you want me to dispose of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time.[�"Are you ready?";You arrive even here undeterred… but not unforeseen."uYou have heeded Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, keepin' a lady waitin' like that."5Hah! Ain’t talkin' 'bout myself – meant Yez."qDon'tcha gimme that smile. She’s right fine when she’s dolled up, and more than that, she’s my friend."5You’re gonna give her your respect, y'hear me?"xNow, got some bad news for ya: I ain’t lettin' you have your last dance with her if I can help it. This ends now."OGlad to hear ya hearin' me. Now, kid, I ain’t 'bout to pull any punches."L'Cause you’re sweet and oh-so-polite, I ain’t gonna break anything."}But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid."6Ah, you’re such a babyface. Real cute one, too."nKinda kid you take home to meet your parents, y’know? Shame I’m gonna have to put you six feet under.">Hah! I kid, I kid – I ain’t doin’ wetwork. Anymore."OI ain’t lettin’ you get away without a few bruises, though. Ready? Go!"LHey – listen, she’s – don’tcha try goin’ and flusterin’ me."gHad to haul that girl to prom, mind ya, and she wears a nice dress a mite better than yours truly."XMy point is that’s she’s a right fine lady, and ya better respect her like one."IAgh, ya got me distracted. Quit with the psyops and fight me proper."WHah! Whatever you say, kid. I ain’t 'bout to take that metaphor and run with it."\You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliche but that’s my line about it."@I guess ya could say I’m reserving the first dance.  Hah!"AI like you, kid. C’mere. Lemme beat that humor out of you."�Hello there. You arrived just a teensy bit earlier than I expected – I was writing a poem, see. Never to be finished, tragically."�These black arches of stone like a starless sky will soon be replaced by brilliant alabaster, which, well, ruins the central symbolism."GWhat a shame. I assume you’re going to force me to duel you now?"UYou march into my demesne, hauling your well- trained combat creatures with you."�We’ve fought before. You’re completely opposed to my beautiful dream. And you still want to claim I have a choice in the matter?"aDon’t insult me. You’ve made your choice, and now we have to deal with the consequences."^Ah, well. At least you’re honest. I like that about you.  You’ve got such... clarity."�What a gleaming light in this dreary cave. Why, that could almost be poetic! If only we had a hopeless romantic to write that down."QAlas, I’ll be too busy directing my passions into carving your team apart."]Of course! You’re such a brilliant spark in this region.  You deserve odes... sonnets."�On the other hand, the fact that you’re here now against me instead of alongside me means that you’re not as special as I thought."NNo faith. It’s a shame, really! I don’t want to do this!  But I will."4And, since I have to... might as well enjoy it."JWhat? You think a poetic soul is creepy? Does true faith disturb you?"MGenuine emotions uncompromised by the endless drudgery of society? Fine!"VEnjoy where that narrow-minded view gets you.  Namely: here, about to lose to me."Hello, friend."DWe have already begun. Regigigas will quickly remake the world."[I understand that you are here to face Yezera, but unfortunately I can’t allow that."�There is a non-zero chance of your success, and I am not a gambler. If you would like, we can both stay here and talk until the reversion overtakes us."FI supposed as much. Excuse me, but in that case I must fight you."gUniversal knowledge is approaching. I would like to be there to witness it – alone, if possible."cI do not either. Unfortunately, I can tell from your tone that we are, in fact, about to duel."zI am unwilling to let you go further, and I am unwilling to lose. Please understand... and please consider conceding."QThat is the most I am willing to say pertaining to your odds against Yezera."�She is conventionally regarded as unbeatable when she applies herself, though I am aware that you have broken that convention repeatedly."INow, may we end the discussion of theory and add another data point?"OExcuse my verbosity. If you would like to go straight to our duel, we can."gI would not insult your intelligence by pretending we will not fight. That much should be evident."Shall we?"=Oh, uh, hey. Listen: I’m gonna cut right to the chase."2You beat me once. You beat Yezera, um, a lot."mThough, some of those don’t really count, 'cause she was using someone else’s team and – whatever."`Point is, I can’t beat you. But… I gotta try. I’ve got a lot to answer for, y’know?"\Lotta little things I did that I got to make up for. Can’t you just let me have this?"BOf course you can’t. Can’t let me have anything, can you?"bUgh, I was gonna be Champion! I was really gunning for it, too. And then... yeah. Everything."dYou completely overshadow me in every way. I can’t beat you. But I’m gonna try to hurt you."cMaybe to you. But not to them – not to Pokémon.  They’re the ones who have to forgive me."~It’s time for them to stop taking orders and start being treated like equals. That includes from ace trainers like you."_I know you can’t stand that, so... I guess we gotta fight. Sorry... but I’m not sorry."-I don’t. Not most of the time anyways."jI’m trying my best to make things right. Can you say the same? Going around keeping the status quo?"hIs this the world you want? I guess you’re a rich brat, so... yeah. Life’s easy, life’s good."IHmph. I’m gonna try and make it a little harder for you, if I can."+Sorry. Guess I’m a spiteful bastard."yNo! I’ll fail – I’ll gladly fail – but I’m not about to give up.  I’ve got friends that need protecting."cI’ve got stuff in my past I need to make up for. And I’ve got a world that needs building."A better one – one that’s more equal, more fair. Sorry it isn’t what you want, but I won’t just roll over for you."You ready?"& ...Hey. So, uh, this is it, huh?"]You’re, like, not gonna have a change of mind? No justice? No fairness? No punishment?"Oh, who am I kidding – you’re Tamarind’s lapdog.  You’ve been doing her dirty work since, like, literally day one!"8Guess what that means! That’s right: time to pay!"{That’s what they all said. You’re not a team grunt!  You’re just, like, a temporarily inconvenienced mastermind!"dUgh, you’re all the same. Well, I’ve chewed through a lotta grunts. No different this time!"'Nope! But I really really want to!"zTamarind’s out of my reach, but you’re, like, the second-best thing. So c’mere so I can give you a bloody nose."7If you were sorry you’d stop fighting me, idiot!"�You’re such a – such a dolt! How can I get it through your thick skull that you’re the bad guy? Can I beat it into you? Wanna find out?"�Oh, I swear, I’ll roll up these sleeves and deck you myself if I have to! I swear, if you chip my nails I’m gonna kill you for real!"=C’mon, boys and girls! We’ve got a beatdown to give!"Ah. Hah. Hahaha!"}So be it! My reading is complete – the scars of this battle left in the ancient stone here are a portent of things to come."TCan you suppose what it says? It says I shall lose here, and you shall triumph.".Hah! Fate has a sense of humor, it seems."`Go on. Continue yet deeper. I know my place, and will not stand against destiny any longer."qFor my sanity, I will refrain from attempting to divine the results of your future battles. I take my leave."%Awww, kid, you shouldn’t have."xGoin’ all-out? On yours truly? I’m touched. Not even half-honest, either – it’s a treat seein’ you fight."~Go on. Yez is waitin’ for you. I ain’t too hung up on this whole scheme. Yez’ll turn out fine either way – tough girl."RTougher than me, I swear. So you go do what ya got planned, whatever that is."WIf ya hurt her, they’ll never find the body, blah blah blah, you know the drill."AGood luck, kid. Come find me some time afterwards, y’hear?"0...Go. Leave. Now, before I lose my temper."dIs that really what the fate of the universe hangs on? Our relative skill in training Pokémon?"fIt’s ridiculous! It’s idiotic! I can’t believe – go! Just go! I should... I should... go."~Noted. Excuse me – I fear I may not have provided adequate resistance. I now find myself lacking any means to challenge you."m...Understood. I have no recourse but to retreat. I wish you the worst of luck in your future endeavors."KIf you will permit me to leave, I will no longer impede your progress."4Goodbye, friend. I hope never to see you again."Damn it. Damn it!"UI – yeah, that’s how it goes. Never was as good as you. Any of you hotshots."gPushed my Pokémon hard to try and get there, and now look at me. Trying to make up for all of it.":Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Manaphy. I guess that was it."VLet’s get y’all back to a Pokécenter, OK? Get you fixed up... I’m sorry..."AUgh! I’m – fine! Ow. I think I took a stray shot... oof."�Look me in the damn eyes, you dumb grunt! If I was – ow – if I wasn’t... if I wasn’t... I’m feeling a little lightheaded."RIs this why they black out after losing...? I’m gonna... I can’t do this."fGo do whatever it is you think you’re, like, actually accomplishing. You stupid, stupid dolt..."{But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put 'em up, kid."]You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliché but that’s my line about it."9Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Phione. I guess that was it.")I should’ve known she was useless."jYezera was THIS close. So close to getting everything she wanted. All she had to do was not tell you."}She had to not be human. Her one redeeming quality: her inhumanity. And now she went and betrayed that, and with it, me."0Apparently. It’s sickening, to be honest."tThe same shallow, stupid desires as everyone else. I guess I’m just as much of an idiot for believing in her."Yes. Good. For. Her."fUnfortunately, it isn’t so good for her grand plan, nor mine. I hope the catharsis is worth it."5Yes, she did. I’m glad you’ve realized that."(Fine. I hope I never see you again."HBut, well, I’ll take care of her once the regression is complete.";You, on the other hand, I’ll deal with now. So long."XDo you want me to dispose of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time.;[�"Are you ready?";You arrive even here undeterred… but not unforeseen."uYou have heeded Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, ke