e of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time.00Iu;␀>,[[]"	\PN."gY’know, I pretty much assumed this was going to be a trap, but I didn’t think you’d be here.",Well... whatcha doing? Care to explain?"7What? You want me to explain this? Velenz? *shrug*">Oh, I know. But you’re the one standing in front of me."LCute. Never should’ve brought a hero here. Heroes are always trouble.")*snort* Sure, kid. Whatever you say."vI know you’re here with that girl – Candy? Helena’s had her trackers keeping an eye on her for a while now."JShe hasn’t been causing too much trouble, though, so we let her go."dListen, we ran this region. Do you know what that means – taken any political science lately?"JIt means a monopoly on violence. Every government works the same way."BOh, you can call me a tyrant if you want, but I’m no thief."Yep! And a damn good one."fNot an absolute one, though – Andris and Helena made up the other two corners of that triangle."JNot to mention the extensive bureaucracy of Team Chasm at its height."@From who? This was a lawless frontier before we came along."VOnly holdouts like Novo truly resisted unification into the larger establishment."hThe benefits of being a tyrant. If people are getting in the way, you can convince them to... stop."/C’mon. You were raised better than that."8We still rule the region because we ARE the region."�We’ve got old grunts everywhere who’ll still follow orders if I give them. Helena has her trackers, so we’ve got an intelligence agency."dAnd she’s got her claws in LuxTech’s outpost here, so economic development is guided by us."XWe were a big organization. All-encompassing. And we had to be: lots of work to do."uOver just a few decades, we imposed law on this place, created entire new settlements, made it rich and vibrant."�We quintupled the population. We dealt with outbreaks, infighting, earthquakes. We secured the support of multiple major companies."~And at the end of the day, we managed to go legit, integrate with the Prizcan government, and aren’t even hated for it."_If you want to try and do even a tenth of that without resorting to violence, be my guest."�We punished people, which you’d call assault. We imprisoned them, which you’d call kidnapping. We taxed them, which you’d call theft."FOh, sure, people resisted us, but we only acted how a state does."ECandy’s too young to have been around during Chasm’s zenith."~She’s got a child’s notion of justice, and she thinks that performing her own little acts of violence fixes anything."GMaybe she should ask herself why almost everyone’s fine with us."	Yes."Andris did it for money."Helena did it for power."WAnd I did it so I could finally have the resources to properly research the Regis."ZEveryone in Team Chasm – in any organization – has their own reasons to be there."F...We can argue all day, kid. You’re not going to get anywhere."Let me put it this way:"�a lot of the Pokémon Candy has “rescued” were given to Chasm grunts for combat purposes, but they ended up liking their new home plenty fine."PMaybe talking things out would’ve resolved things better than theft, huh?"gBut I know you want to know. What’s up with Velenz? Well, it’s simple. We were trying to work."�I can’t work when I’m being attacked by wannabe heroes. When the power grid is being fried. When Ghost-types are being sent to haunt my lab.";We asked, repeatedly, for them to stop. They didn’t."tSo I took Regigigas and had it carve up the bedrock around here, then dragged some avatars in for good measure."zThey couldn’t prove it was us, but pretty soon they lost their base of operations, and that got the message across."LYes. Was. If they’d wanted to keep it, they could’ve left us alone."?Kid, have you ever gotten twelve hours of sleep in a week?"vThese “freedom fighters” were using every trick in the book. Constantly harrying us. Never a moment’s rest.".Ugh. Makes me mad just thinking about it."I think so, yeah."NThat’s how it goes. Warfare ain’t pretty, but it exists for a reason."qI did what I did. And if someone wants to “bring me to justice” for it, I say: what does that even mean?"LI’m breaking my back running this region, making it better every day."fYou want to throw me in prison? Make this place worse so you can have your petty revenge? Idiocy."SI know what I did, and I’m not going to do it again. Neither is anyone else."|...Now, kid. I need to get out of this place, because I don’t particularly want to run into Candy. Get out of my way."NYou need to work on your active listening. I didn’t ask you a question."MI told you what you were going to do… and now you’re going to do it."Ugh. Heroes!"3Damn heroes... well, what’d I really expect."Get up."CI’m not angry, just disappointed. But I will be taking my–"\PN! Tamarind!"xStop right there. I – I know I took, um, a little bit to get here, but that’s only because I was eavesdropping!";Candy, is it? Good to meet you in person... I suppose."5You know where I stand. And I know where you do."�I’ve just settled things with \PN, so why don’t we have a chat in private? \PN, be a dear for me and leave us. I’d like to end this grudge here and now."Z...Alright. This is between you and me, anyways. \PN, you can go, like, wait outside."+Just for a minute. This’ll be quick.".Good. Glad we can see eye to eye on this."You first."Not my idea."Getting answers."Delivering justice."Tyrant."You seized power."And Velenz?"You don't rule anymore."Not just violence."Some hate you."You did it for yourself."It was their home."That seems excessive."Fair enough."..."No."...Alright.[]"	\PN."gY’know, I pretty much assumed this was going to be a trap, but I didn’t think you’d be here.",Well... whatcha doing? Care to explain?"7What? You want me to explain this? Velenz? *shrug*">Oh, I know. But you’re the one standing in front of me."LCute. Never should’ve brought a hero here. Heroes are always trouble.")*snort* Sure, kid. Whatever you say."vI know you’re here with that girl – Candy? Helena’s had her trackers keeping an eye on her for a while now."JShe hasn’t been causing too much trouble, though, so we let her go."dListen, we ran this region. Do you know what that means – taken any political science lately?"JIt means a monopoly on violence. Every government works the same way."BOh, you can call me a tyrant if you want, but I’m no thief."Yep! And a damn good one."fNot an absolute one, though – Andris and Helena made up the other two corners of that triangle."JNot to mention the extensive bureaucracy of Team Chasm at its height."@From who? This was a lawless frontier before we came along."VOnly holdouts like Novo truly resisted unification into the larger establishment."hThe benefits of being a tyrant. If people are getting in the way, you can convince them to... stop."/C’mon. You were raised better than that."8We still rule the region because we ARE the region."�We’ve got old grunts everywhere who’ll still follow orders if I give them. Helena has her trackers, so we’ve got an intelligence agency."dAnd she’s got her claws in LuxTech’s outpost here, so economic development is guided by us."XWe were a big organization