ey’re paying you to be here."jTeam Chasm apparently had roots in anthropology, based on all the records they’ve shoved away here."_Translated passages with way too many sticky notes go over all kinds of myths and legends."\One that caught my eye involves the Seekers, those ancient priests I mentioned earlier."tThey were ultimately destroyed by a great darkness that some protector deity was apparently equipped to handle."dBut, based on the fact that the Seekers disappeared, the guardian must have failed in its duty."Why? I don’t know."ZThe notes here make reference to materials that I can’t find anywhere in this room."?I’m thinking that these records have to exist elsewhere."�And I’m going to assume that they must have been saved digitally, as there’s nowhere else in the region with this much literature."mDo you think you can search LuxTech for any servers hosting data from before Team Chasm was established?"VI’ll keep on searching here in the meantime for something hidden in the stacks."7Let me know if you find something over at LuxTech."PI’ve only been finding fun facts, the kind you’d see on a moving truck."IDid you know that hexagons were an important symbols of the Seekers?";That’s apparently what inspired Team Chasm’s logo."You’re back! Excellent.":I managed to make a breakthrough while you were away."9Would you mind showing me what you’ve found first?"%You hand over the Old USB Drive.")Nora loads the device on her laptop."Fascinating."�This one file, Project Chrysopoeia Albedo, goes into great detail of a large volcanic eruption thousands of years ago which heavily impacted the region."uIt makes sense that the large clouds of ash would be devastating to a civilization in its technological infancy."BThis must be the "great darkness" that the Seekers mentioned."qPerhaps that’s also why they built what would become the underground ruins; like those found in Mt. Kilna?"CMaybe those places were meant to be safe spaces from the smog?"KWait, no. Why would they have built shelters if they had the guardian?"2Hahaha. This is the rush I’ve been seeking."0Questions whose answers are more questions."tAs for my own findings: I found references to an aboveground ruins site which might lead to what we’re after."GI’ll be waiting for you in <imp>Svait, on the upper level</imp>."6A beautifully illuminated religious-looking text."7The script looks familiar, but not enough to read."A regal figure.";According to the plaque, it's the First King of Makya."4Very torn looking books. Better not touch them."BAh, please don't touch those. I'm sending them in for repair."1You'd be surprised how brittle these can be.[:"8Leather- and cloth-bound books are neatly lined up."CYou can't imagine how much it would cost if they were damaged."KAn old, beaten up laptop. A couple dozen windows are open all at once."RSomething is being researched, but it's impossible to tell what specifically."QIt's Nora's laptop. She must have forgotten it in her hurry to get to Svait."XA map displayed on the screen shows a path to the west of the Ranger Station there."q“Over 2500 years ago, there existed a sect of itinerant priests who worshipped a Legendary Carver of Clay."^And by its hand, people were able to claim dominion over inhospitable lands high and low."sYet, despite their efforts, humanity was cast out from the lands where the primal forces of this world worked."gBack to the caves; which their species used to call home. Now the caverns would be their tombs…""sGuess I forgot to keep the door locked… but I can’t really turn away the esteemed Champion \PN, now can I?"sI don’t know why you’re here but, if I had to make a guess… you’re searching for something; like I am."GName’s Nora. I like to think of myself as a seeker of knowledge."mI took up a job as a janitor here to gain access to this library, since it’s sealed off to the public."?It’s not trespassing if they’re paying you to be here."jTeam Chasm apparently had roots in anthropology, based on all the records