 site which might lead to what we’re after."GI’ll be waiting for you in <imp>Svait, on the upper level</imp>."6A beautifully illuminated religious-looking text."7The script looks familiar, but not enough to read."A regal figure.";According to the plaque, it's the First King of Makya."4Very torn looking books. Better not touch them."BAh, please don't touch those. I'm sending them in for repair."1You'd be surprised how brittle these can be.Iu;␀�[[/";Wow! It's a Volcanion, trapped inside a large boulder!"(Hey, \PN! Come around to the front."~It’s still so striking to me that at any time, Team Chasm could’ve added this protector of the region to its arsenal."oSure, they managed to capture Heatran, the Titans, and other oddities I still need to comb that USB about."cBut were they so dominated by Yezera that they thought Volcanion wouldn’t make a difference?"eIt makes me realize how terrifying going against a single person with overwhelming power can be."...as you showed me, \PN."Anyway, ready?">Nora brings out a small MP3 player, and presses a button."<A soothing recording of an ancient flute fills the air."IAh. Seems like we have unwanted guests at this once private concert."6Awesome. At least they look in the mood to dance."SI guess we can crack some heads open, show them a genuine mosh pit experience."What do you think, \PN?"qAh. I realize now that, while I patched your team up after our battle, I’m out of supplies to heal my own."I’ll be counting on you!"What a painful cry…"�I can’t imagine how it must feel to wake up thousands of years after the disappearance of the people you were meant to protect."QI realize now that I’ve only thought about how others would USE Volcanion."6As a tool, a reward, or something in that vein…";I haven't been seeing this creature as a living being."!I saw it as words on a page."7Volcanion seems to be looking to you for guidance."Take Volcanion with you?"ENora, seeing your intent, comes over and hands you a Poké Ball."AThe Vo