aken by the target."WThe user charges by gathering light, then blasts all near foes on the second turn."�The user heals all non-volatile status conditions on their side, gains the ability Stability, heals itself for 25% HP and becomes Grass-type."IThe user inflicts leech on all nearby foes. User becomes Grass-type."hThe user raises its Defense by two steps and gains the ability Iron Barbs. User becomes Grass-type."]The user scatters bursts of spores to induce sleep on all foes. User becomes Grass-type."The user summons an allied Gossifleur. This raises its Sp. Def by three steps, and its allies' by one. User becomes Grass-type."FA powerful electric blast is let loose on the target, numbing it."TThe user raises its Sp. Atk and Speed by two steps. User becomes Electric-type."KThe user inflicts numb on all nearby foes. User becomes Electric-type."TTwo turns after this move is used, a hunk of psychic energy attacks the target."hThe user raises its Sp. Def by four steps and gains the ability Unaware. User becomes Psychic-type."pThe user raises its Sp. Atk and Sp. Def by two steps and maximizes its Accuracy. User becomes Psychic-type."kThe user summons eclipse for six turns. This raises its Attack and Sp. Atk. User becomes Psychic-type."SBounces back status moves for the next three turns. User becomes Psychic-type."{The user summons an allied Abra. This raises its Sp. Atk by three steps, and its allies' by one. User becomes Psychic-type."bThe user creates an Odd Room for six turns. This raises its Speed. User becomes Psychic-type."}The user employs hypnotic suggestion to make all nearby statused foes fall into a deep sleep. User becomes Psychic-type."OThe target is struck with an absolute zero beam of energy, frostbiting it."NThe user inflicts frostbite on all nearby foes. User becomes an Ice-type."_The user lays two hazard layers of frozen spikes on the foe's side. User becomes Ice-type."lThe user summons hail for six turns. This lowers every foe's Speed by two steps. User becomes Ice-type."XThe user raises its Attack, Defense, and Speed by two steps. User becomes Ice-type."The user crushes all near foes with evil intent. This deals double damage to targets with a non-volatile status condition."NThe user exhales a mighty gust that inflicts damage and numbs the target."sA move that only the avatar of Zekrom can use. All battlers gain Steel-type and have their stat changes reset."QThe user raises its Attack and Speed by two steps. User becomes Dragon-type."ZThe user lowers each near foe's highest stat by four steps. User becomes Dragon-type."oA move that only the avatar of Reshiram can use. All battlers have all of their stats raised by two steps."|The user summons an allied Poochyena. This raises its Attack by three steps, and its allies' by one. User becomes Dark-type."cThe user torments all near foes, preventing them from repeating moves. User becomes Dark-type."gThe user blasts all nearby foes with the moon's full power, lowering their Sp. Atk by three steps."HThe user raises its Sp. Atk by four steps. User becomes Fairy-type."yThe user summons moonglow for six turns. This raises the Defense and Sp. Def of all allies. User becomes Fairy-type."oThe user creates a Puzzle Room for six turns. This raises its Attack and Sp. Atk. User becomes Fairy-type."AThis move exists just to showcase the PBS Extensions system.;[�"NThe user helps the target and makes it use its move right after the user."bThe user hurriedly and randomly uses a move among those known by other Pokémon in the party."EThe user maximizes its Attack in exchange for 33% of its max HP."WThe user passes its held item to the target when the target isn't holding an item."`The user endures attacks for two turns, then strikes back to cause double the damage taken."UThe user traps the target by physically blocking its way or scaring it in place."[The user drops onto the target with its full body weight. It has a 30% chance to numb."eThe user attacks everything around it with the destructive power of a terrible, explosive sound."KThe user changes its type to become the same type as one of its moves."iThe user changes its type to make itself resistant to the type of the attack the opponent used last."hThe user approaches the target, then steals their item. Items stolen from wild Pokémon are stored."ZThe target is hit with rhythmically launched punches that have a 30% chance to dizzy."EA reckless, life-risking tackle. The user also takes 33% recoil."mThe user attacks the foe with an echoing voice. If this move is used every turn, it does greater damage."ZThe user compels the target to keep using only the move it last used for three turns."JAn attack move that cuts down the target's HP to equal the user's HP."aThe user endures any attack with at least 1 HP. It always fails if it is used in succession."jThe user dances to compel the target to mimic it, making the target's Ability the same as the user's."bThe user explodes to inflict damage on those around it. The user faints upon using this move."aThe user rushes the target at blinding speed. This attack always goes before any other move."xDoubles its power if the user has a non-volatile status condition. Ignores damage reduction from burn or frostbite."oAn attack that hits first and makes the target flinch. It only works the first turn the user is in battle."bThe user flails about aimlessly to attack. It becomes more powerful the less HP the user has."WEnables random critical hits for the user, and quadruples its critical hit chance."eThe user draws attention to itself, making all foes' moves get redirected to the user this turn."[The target is multi-hit two to five times with raking swipes. Can random critical hit."hThe user rushes at the target using every bit of its power. The user is exhausted on the next turn."GThe user intimidates the target by staring at it to cause numbing."PThe user growls, scaring nearby foes. Their Attack is lowered by two steps."WThe user stiffens all the muscles in its body to raise its Defense by three steps."dThe user sticks out its head and attacks by slamming into the foe. It has a 50% chance to numb."oThe user makes a soothing bell chime to heal the non-volatile status conditions of all the party Pokémon."NThe user assists an ally by boosting the power of its next attack by 50%."TThe user holds back when it attacks, and the target is left with at least 1 HP."VThe foe is attacked with a powerful beam. The user is exhausted on the next turn."fThe user bites hard on the target with its sharp fangs. It has a 50% chance to flinch the target."SThe user lets loose a horribly echoing shout with the power to inflict damage."lThe user releases countless shots of light. Its type varies with the kind of Plate the user is holding."cThis move can be used only after the user has used all the other moves it knows in the battle."ZThe user leers at nearby foes with sharp eyes. Their Defense is lowered by two steps."~If the user acts before the target, it copies the target’s attacking move and uses it against them with 50% increased power."FThe target is slugged by a punch thrown with muscle-packed power."\The user waggles a finger and stimulates its brain into randomly using nearly any move."qCloaking itself in high energy, the user slams into the target. This move's type depends on the held memory."^The user draws power to attack by using a held Berry. The Berry used determines its type."oAn attack that makes use of nature's power. Its effects and type vary depending on the user's environment."ZThe user intimidates all nearby foes, lowering their Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps."ONumerous coins are hurled at the target to inflict damage. Scatters coins."IThe target is physically pounded with a long tail or a foreleg, etc."NIt enables the user to evade all attacks. It fails if used in succession."iThe user lunges at the target at a speed that makes it almost invisible. It is sure to strike first."sA spin attack that can also e