ngs to pummel the target. Skips and destroys protections."\The user summons bugs to terrorize the target, trapping and binding it for three turns."YThe user amps itself up for performance, raising its Sp. Atk and Speed by two steps."hTwo turns after this move is used, the target's HP is restored by three quarters the user's max HP."|The user goes into another plane and displaces the target's soul. This move does 30% more damage if the user is asleep."lDisables the target's last used move for four turns, then lowers a relevant stat on them by four steps."oThe user attacks with bitter emotion. This lowers the target's Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps if in hail."WThe user causes a glitch in reality. This attack always results in a critical hit."`The user loses 25% of their max HP to curse the target, damaging their HP by 25% each turn."dThe user makes a dreadful bell noise, harming all near battlers with visions of impending doom."LThe target becomes trapped, and takes 50% more damage from all attacks."aThe user sings with deathly sounds to harm the target. It has a 20% chance to lower Sp. Def."]The target is subjected to a violent and frightening prank. It has a 10% chance to numb."iThe user forces itself or the target to spend 25% HP to make a Substitute by turning it into a doll."hThe user soothes the target, lowering its Speed by four steps. If in hail, they also become drowsy."vThe user channels its fallen allies to strike the target. This attack has 20 more power per fainted party member."PDisables the target's last used move for five turns, and cuts 5 PP from it."mSpectral hands reach from the ground to trip the target. The heavier the target, the greater the damage."gThe user foretells a terrifying danger. Two turns later, the targeted spot is mortally frightened."`Changes type based on machine haunted. 30% chance of extra effect based on machine haunted."jThe user cleanses the target's impurities with spiritual energy. Super effective versus Poison-types."DThe user switches out using a cruel illusion. Always goes last."pThe user opens its soul to unleash massive energy. This lowers the user's Sp. Atk and Sp. Def by two steps."{The target begins transforming into gold. They lose 1/8th HP every turn, scattering ten times as many coins as health lost."yThe user makes the target hit itself by possessing its body. This move does 50% more damage if the target is asleep."iThe user summons apparitions that dance around hypnotically before they multi-hit two to five times."gThe user practices its punches against ghostly illusions, raising its Attack, Speed, and Accuracy."WThe user drains heat from the air around the target, afflicting it with frostbite."OThe user buries the target with somber force. Then, this move is disabled."pThe user drains the target's soul. The user's HP is restored by 50% of the damage dealt. This can overheal."XThe user licks the target, numbing them, or cursing them if they're already numbed."gThe user unleashes its grudge, damaging the target and cutting 4 PP from the move last used by it."MThe user heals itself by 66% of its max HP. Then, this move is disabled."aThe user suffocates the target by sucking the air from their lungs. Can random critical hit."oThe user snips the target's connection to life in order to curse them, damaging their HP by 25% each turn."aThe user thins the air around the target, depriving them of oxygen. Can random critical hit."PThe target is pestered by a giant tongue. This has a 50% chance to numb it."fThe user shoots the target with darkness formed from anger. It has a 40% chance to lower Sp. Def."jThe user rips into the target's soul, dealing damage through their Sp. Def rather than their Defense."NThe user attacks while wailing. It has a 40% chance to flinch the target."VThe user channels the anger of wronged spirits, going on a rampage for two turns."aThe user slashes with gusto, inspiring its allies to follow up by using Slash on the target."ZThe user uses gunpowder to rocket at its foe. It has a 30% chance to raise its Speed."\A reckless maneuver that forces the user to switch out if it misses. Always goes first."vInflicts physical or special damage, whichever deals more. Then, raises Attack or Sp. Atk, whichever wasn't used."VConductive materials ensnare the target, trapping and binding it for three turns."nThe user launches piercing feathers three times, lowering the foe's Defense. Then, this move is disabled."nThe user lays a levitating hazard of sharp feathers around the foe. It deals Steel-typed 1/8th HP damage."The user dislodges a blast of thin projectiles. This attack always results in a critical hit, but applies fracture to the user."uThe user uses explosive force to shoot shards of its own body at the target. The user loses 1/8th of its max HP."]The user reflects a burst of light off its curls. Blinds a Pokémon entering the battle."_The user headbutts the target with a metal head. It has a 40% chance to flinch the target."�A large spike is shot at the target. If this causes the target to faint, a hazard layer of Spikes is set on the ground beneath them."LThe target is pierced with a sharp iron arrow. Can random critical hit."QThe target is pierced with a pointed metal javelin. Can random critical hit."QThe user attacks with reflected light. It has a 20% chance to lower Sp. Def."_The user strikes the target while magnetizing it, trapping and binding it for three turns."LProtects the user from attacks. Special attackers take 1/8th HP damage."YThe user attacks the target with a sword. If the target faints, scatters many coins."�The user creates a high quality area for six turns in which super-effective deals 25% more, and not very effective deals 25% less."aThe user creates an explosion from powdered metal, inflicting damage to all nearby battlers."4The user strikes with a full-force hammer blow."bThe user shoots a massive metal object at the target. The user is exhausted on the next turn."UThe user economizes half of its weight, healing itself based on the weight lost."WThe user launches a fist with extreme force. This attack is popular with children."|The user lines up shards before attacking. If hit by a foe's special move, lays a hazard layer of Spikes at their feet."jThe user crushes the target in its metallic vises, breaking any screens protecting the target's side."dThe user looses a flash of energy from its polished body. It has a 40% chance to lower Sp. Def."kProtects the user from damage this turn. It also lowers the Sp. Atk of special attackers by two steps."/The user hurls a metal ball at the target."^The user shoots shards of its own body at the target. The user loses 1/8th of its max HP."jThe user shreds off bits of its own body to launch at the target. The user loses 1/8th of its max HP."OThe user sprays mining waste at the target. It has a 30% chance to poison."\The user slashes at the target with a steel blade. Super effective versus Dragon-types."aThe user heals itself by half of their max HP. This extends the current weather by one turn."WThe user enters a protective stance, raising its Sp. Atk and Defense by two steps."QHits once for each party Pokémon. Deals more damage based on their Sp. Atk."ZThe user prepares its dual cannons. Until switch out, each special attack hits twice."[The user drags the target into the water with a heavy anchor. They become waterlogged."fWelds heavy steel onto the target, giving it the Steel type and lowering its Speed by four steps."oCharges by summoning sunshine for five turns, then overwhelms the foe with fiery light on the second turn."eThe user rushes the target at blazing-fast speed. This attack always goes before any other move."cThe user attacks by sending a wave of hot air towards the target. It has a 30% chance to burn."yGuaranteed to critical hit if the target has stat step changes. The target is cleansed, reseting their stat changes."QThe foe is engulfed in a firestorm, trapping and binding it for three turns."\The target is dried out and loses Water-type. Then, it bursts into flame from the heat."]The user emits great amounts of heat, burning the target and adding the Fire-type to it."aThe user fires off explosive rounds in a beautiful display that multi-hit two to five times."aThe target is punched with a tremendous fiery force. This move can't be used twice in a row."zThe user lays a hazard layer of burning spikes on the foe's side. One layer hurts switched in foes, two layers burns."VThe user flashes with a burst of intensely bright flame. Can random critical hit."nThe user targets the opponents soft spots with a fiery strike. Its power doubles if the target is burned."gRaises Sp. Atk by three steps. Until switch out, the user's attacks spread to hit all nearby foes."The user creates a golden pyre that revives a fainted Pokémon at half HP. That Pokémon switches in and its stats are boosted."sThe user dances with great heat. Pokémon hit by this are cured of frostbite. Deals 50% less damage to allies."mThe user pauses to plan its ranged attacks. This raises its Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Accuracy by two steps."WThe user shoots the target with a small bolt of fire. This move always goes first."9The user sets the target on fire, inflicting a burn."�If the target has a non-volatile status condition, this deals double damage and heals every battler's non-volatile status condition."^The user cloaks itself in a fierce blaze and attacks. It has a 20% chance to raise Speed."JThe user burns the target, then welcomes in sunshine for eight turns."TThe user warms up its body and attacks the target. It has a 10% chance to burn."wThe user launches up high, charging and becoming hidden, then explodes down on the second turn, taking 25% recoil."pThe user roars with the force of a volcano, raising the Attack of itself by three steps and allies' by one."kThe user attacks with fire that can be seen in multiple places, then summons sunshine for eight turns."{A lance of fire pierces the target from above, lowering their Sp. Atk. Can random critical hit, and does so twice as often."dThe user explodes itself into the target. The target is harmed, but also their Speed is raised."[Halves attack damage taken this turn. Burns any attackers. Fails if used successively."yThe user chomps down with burning fangs. It has a 20% chance to burn and a 20% chance to lower Defense by two steps."nThe user attacks with heat, creating an obscuring wall of haze. The user takes 33% less damage this turn."QCloaked in flames, the user dances wildly, raising its Sp. Atk by two steps."�The user sends up to two barrages of fire, each hitting two to five times. If two barrages were sent, the user is exhausted on the next turn."ZSummons sunshine for six turns, boosting Fire-type attacks and hindering most others."vThe user launches volcanic debris, dealing damage and setting a hazard layer of burning spikes around the target."aThe user surrounds the target with fire which also destroys any clothing items it's holding."gA distinguished attack that motivates nearby allies to follow, letting them act immediately after."cThe user launches a concentrated ball of searing, bright white flame. Can random critical hit."}The user creates a storm using its flaming body, damaging everything around it and melting away hazards from both sides."oThe user rapidly changes water pressure, creating a pulsing shockwave. The user loses 1/8th of its max HP."vThe user bites with watery fangs. It has a 20% chance to waterlog and a 20% chance to lower Defense by two steps."jCharges by summoning rainstorm for five turns, then overwhelms the foe with water on the second turn."oThe user shoots purified water, also healing the non-volatile status conditions of all the party Pokémon."RThe user jumps out of the water to attack. Has a 20% chance to lower Defense."cThe user creates numerous bubbles to explode against the target. Multi-hits two to five times."�The user creates a bubble to shield their ally. The next time they're hit, 50% of the move damage is instead dealt back as recoil."_A blast of bubbles is shot at the target. It has a 20% chance to lower the target's Speed."A water vacuum is induced and rapidly collapsed, generating an intense pulsing water blast. The user loses 1/8th of its max HP."fThe user pulls the target under the waves with crushing force. This has a 10% chance to waterlog."TThe user douses the target, healing itself by 33% of its max HP in the process."�The user spews alkaline bubbles that melt the target. For the next two turns, the target's Defense will be lowered by two steps."_Halves attack damage taken this turn. Waterlogs any attackers. Fails if used successively."\The user struggles in the water, splashing it onto the target. They become waterlogged."dThe user gains an instinctual knowledge of battle, raising its Attack and Sp. Def by two steps."UThe user crashes into the target with its quills. It leaves the target poisoned."oThe user propels a geyser of water at the target. This lowers the user's Sp. Atk and Sp. Def by two steps."lThe user dives down with its beak wide open. Transforms into Gulping- or Gorging form, depending on HP."UThe user crashes into the target like a tsunami. The user also takes 33% recoil."HThe target is immersed in water. This has a 30% chance to waterlog."OThe user waterlogs the target, then welcomes in rainstorm for eight turns."wThe user opens a spring to blast the target, also forming an Aqua Ring around themselves, healing 10% HP per turn."qAttacks with pressurized water. Deals 50% more damage if the user has been hurt by the foe in the same turn."`The target is struck with a stream of pressurized water. This has a 10% chance to waterlog."\Summons rainstorm for six turns, boosting Water-type attacks and hindering most others."eThe user rams its sharp face right into the target. This lowers the user's Speed by three steps."VThe user crashes into the target on a ripping current. This waterlogs the target."kThe user rips the target, lowering their Defense by two steps. After attacking, the user switches out."SStrikes the target with harbor waters, then summons rainstorm for eight turns."�The user rests in a riverbed, restoring its HP by half of max, and forming an Aqua Ring around themselves, healing 10% HP per turn."�The user communes with all the world's water, waterlogging the target and forming an Aqua Ring around themselves, healing 10% HP per turn."oThe user attacks with a wave of murky water, which hits all near foes and lowers their Speed by two steps."iThe target is crushed in the user's shell, mouth, or claws, trapping and binding it for three turns."cThe user rams the target while splashing up a lot of water. This has a 30% chance to waterlog."dThe target gets covered in sticky spines, waterlogging it and losing 1/8th of their current HP."ZThe user wields tidal power to grab at the target. This has a 10% chance to waterlog."`The user uses a jet of water like a sword and attacks by slashing. Can random critical hit."gThe user wakes to unleash devastating tides. Can only be used while asleep, and wakes the user up."=The target is doused with water in order to waterlog it."mThe user crashes into the target with the force of a large wave. This has a 40% chance to lower Defense."�The user attacks the target using graceful fluid movements, also forming an Aqua Ring around themselves, healing 10% HP per turn."�The user's song heals the non-volatile status conditions of all party Pokémon, and forms an Aqua Ring around itself, healing 10% HP per turn."YThe target is inundated with a wave of seaweater. This has a 30% chance to waterlog."cThe user rides a wave, then crashes into the target. It has a 40% chance to flinch the target."@The user applies anesthetic substances, numbing the target."sThe user uses wind to blast its leaves at the target. This lowers the user's Defense and Sp. Def by two steps."uThe user gracefully slashes the target three times. The next time this move is used, it will hit one extra time."cFlowers bloom with intensity, damaging the target and raising the user's Sp. Atk by two steps."SRevives a fainted Grass-type party member to full HP. Only one use per battle."qThe user fades into the foliage, charging and becoming hidden, then strikes from stealth on the second turn."pThe user drops some heads from high up. The taller the user compared to the target, the greater the damage."nThe user flicks its thorns, dealing damage and setting a hazard layer of poison spikes around the target."eThe user fires a bolt of life energy at the target. It has a 20% chance to raise user's Sp. Atk."RThe target is disoriented by an explosive seed. It has a 30% chance to dizzy."KRound objects are hurled at the target to strike three times in a row."gThe user attacks the target with the power of a warding charm. Super effective versus Ghost-types."�The user keeps time for the team while attacking. Raises user's and allies' Speed and Accuracy. Counts as a Sound and Kick move."sThe user sheathes its blade. If hit by a foe's special move, it unsheathes it quickly, slashing all near foes."^The user uses their feet to pierce the foe. This has a 10% chance of leeching the target."RThe user eats decaying leaves, restoring its HP by 50% and raising its Speed."fThe target eats a strange seed. They become numbed if faster than the user, or leeched if slower."YCreates an odd flower to throw and damage a foe. Odd Room is created for five turns."PThe user stirs up a violent petal tempest and attacks everything around it."@The target is irritated by allergenic plants, poisoning it."oThe user bursts a ball of sleep-inducing powder. It fails unless the targeted slot hit the user this turn."\Attacks all near foes while destroying rooms. This move fails in the absence of a room."]The user kicks into the target like roots into earth. This has a 30% chance of leeching."]Halves attack damage taken this turn. Leeches any attackers. Fails if used successively."gLays roots that heal the user by absorbing 1/8th HP from foes each turn. The user becomes trapped."zSaps an enemy lured into its jaws. If they hit the user this turn, the user's HP is restored by 66% the damage dealt."[Attacks with energy from jealousy. All opposing Pokémon with stat boosts get leeched."PA parasitic seed leeches the target and lowers both its Attack and Sp. Atk."OThe user and the target each share their highest stat step with the other."OAttacks by gliding on the ground. This move always goes first in sunshine."gThe user calms itself and its teammates, raise its Sp. Def by three steps, and its allies' by one."VA nutrient-draining attack. The user's HP is restored by 75% of the damage dealt."aThe user makes a scary sound by shaking, forcing the target to switch out. Always goes last."UThe user wraps the target in its vines, trapping and binding it for three turns."_The user whips their legs into the target like a plant. This has a 10% chance of leeching."|Guaranteed to critical hit if the target has no stat step changes. The target is surged forward, raising all its stats."nThe user assists an ally's next move, boosting its power by 50% and letting it move right after the user."QA flare of electricity creates a bright light, damaging all nearby battlers."TFor the rest of the round, the target's healing is reversed. Always goes first."�The user and the target pit their energy against one another. The damage is based on the target's Sp. Atk rather than their Sp. Def."�The user surges with electricity. If it deals less than 50% of the target's max health, the user takes the difference as recoil."jThe user wraps their body in electricity and crashes into the target. The user also takes 20% recoil."ERevives a fainted party member to 1 HP. Only one use per battle."cThe user breaks down all insulation to send a barrage of electricity to rampage for two turns."rThe user forces electricity between opposite points on the target's body. Super effective versus Steel-types."_The user harnesses a blade of lightning and slices at the target. Can random critical hit."dThe target is punched with a tremendous electric force. This move can't be used twice in a row."PThe user lets out an electric roar, raising the user's Speed by four steps."mThe user slashes all opposing Pokémon with tendrils of electricity, lowering their Attack by two steps."xThe user attacks with courage. Sets a Spikes hazard layer if Full. If Hangry, deals double damage and is Dark-type."rThe user dances to heal an ally by half of their max HP. They're cured of any non-volatile status conditions."jCloaking itself in light energy, the user shocks the target, raising the user's Sp. Def by two steps."SDeals 50% more damage if faster than the target. This lowers the user's Speed."pThe target is pranked by an electric jolt. They are taunted and unable to use status moves for three turns."[The user strikes the enemy while coated with electricity. It has a 10% chance to numb."jElectricity is generated to beam intense light directly at the target. This has a 30% chance to numb."dThe user dances with the speed of lightning, raising its Sp. Atk by two steps and Speed by one."WThe user slams down into the target with electricity. It has a 10% chance to numb."rThe user lays a hazard around the foe. It deals Electric-typed 1/12th HP damage, or double that in rainstorm."ZThe user dances to encourage its ally. Their attacks this turn will be critical hits."�The user coils its body to generate an electric field, levitating for five turns and raising its Attack and Sp. Def by two steps."VA megawatt of electricity surges through the target. It has a 30% chance to numb."[The user finds the highest base power move among your able party members, and uses it."9A weak electric jolt is launched to numb the target."~The user slices with claws of light that have a 50% chance to numb. Can random critical hit. Counts as a Light and Slice move."rSends a pulse to flip the pola