o encounters on this map."Replace Search"Search Nearby"Un-Star Species"Star Species"Do what with this species?"DThis feature of the DexNav is unavailable during this minigame.""Searching\ts[15]...\wtnp[{1}]" Oh! A {1} was found nearby!"DexNav: {1}"SIt's open to a battling guide written by someone with the username "apolLyon.""1.1 Roles/Cores"2.1 Leads"3.2 Hazards"(Which entry would you like to read?"KEverything on your team needs a point. Every Pokémon needs a purpose."PIf you can't sum up its role on your team in a sentence, keep it in the PC."TEvery bit of that Pokémon should reinforce its role. Moves, items, everything."@All six Pokémon on your team need a role, narrow or broad."=Two Pokémon with synergistic roles are called a "core.""\If the two of them can take hits from a whole bunch of things, that's a defensive core."nIf together they threaten lots of Pokémon and deal with each others' counters, that's an offensive core."SCombine both and you have a balanced core. Good cores make for powerful teams."QYou don't need them, but they're a surefire way to give your team some bite."8The Pokémon you start a fight with is your "lead.""OStart every fight with it and it's a "dedicated lead." Make it a good one."@Its job is to kick things off in your favor from round one."dUsually that's by vomiting up a whole bunch of hazards. Sometimes it sets screens and explodes."kA few just try to delete whatever's on the other side, usually with short-term power boosts like Gems."FSpeaking of which, your opponent is going to have their own lead."AStop it. Taunt it, put it to sleep, or put it in the ground."IThe arena is going to very rapidly fill up with nasty pointy things."�That's because wasting a turn setting them up in the short term pays off big in the long term when they chew up a few Pokémon worth of health over the course of the match."tIf you like being alive, pack something that can clean up hazards – Defog, Terraform, or Rapid Spin, usually."uStealth Rocks are the most common hazard, so prioritize hazard removal if you've got lots of Rock-weak Pokémon."�Remember: if your favorite little gremlin is switching out nine times a match or is cripplingly weak to funny pebbles, put Heavy-Duty Boots on it." They're cute and effective."You exit the PC."VIt's open to a battling guide written by someone with the username "snowwhip401.""Even keel"Best foot forward"Rolling with the punches"<All the little pieces of your team need their own role."dUse whatever you want; just ensure that it's got something to do and the best odds of doing it."5Give bulky Pokémon Leftovers and healing moves."IGive strong, slow Pokémon Focus Sashes, Vests, or ways to speed up."You get the idea."aIf you can, try to have all kinds of Pokémon on your team, so you have answers to anything."pPhysical and special bulk and power, type matchups, speed profiles – a diverse team is a diverse toolbox."ISend out the Pokémon that helps everything else on your team first.":If you have a weather or a Room to set up, get to it."EIf you don't have a clear, clean gameplan, ruin your opponent's."wA dedicated lead's worst fear is usually a strong multi-hitting move. Neither Sturdy nor Sash can help them there."}As opposed to simply trading hazards, outspeeding and KOing a lead before it gets going can give you an early advantage."8Each Pokémon's utility is defined by the opponent."ZIf your opponent has several Fire-type Pokémon, your Primarina is far more valuable."0Conserve its health and leverage its power."]In the same match, an Aegislash may be far less valuable – be willing to sacrifice it."ZThere's no shame in letting a Pokémon fall in order to get a safe switch to another."xWhile they may seem drastic, moves such as Healing Wish or Explosion can turn the tide of a match in a single turn."kFainting the user can, if used with finesse, be an advantage – think of them as the ultimate U-Turn."%...The blizzard pushes you back.",The Corviknight stares at you intently."<You get the sense that you've failed some sort of test."Green-thumbed"Savior"Scornful"Grand Design"Treason".<i>Drink the regal blood if you must.</i>"C<i>Indulge in your <b>traitorous nature</b> if you insist.</i>"<i>Repulsive flea...</i>"0<i><b>I will swat you from the sky.</b></i>"7<i>Let this act as a lesson in humility, worm!</i>"<i>What!!?</i>"!<i>How... how could you?</i>"T<i>To think!! My gift to the world, in the hands of the <b>undeserving</b>!</i>"d<i>Insolent fool! Treasonous wretch!!! Usurping the King of All in your desperate attemp–</i>"MCalyrex's protests fade away, leaving an echoing silence in its absence."#I'm energized and ready to go!"ZI don't spend my energy needlessly. Grab me a Sweet Heart and I'll consider battling."So, you got one?"FWow, you actually did it. With this much energy, I'm unstoppable!"?It's much too cold in here to battle without a pick-me-up."HThey're the Skeevee Eevee specialty. Where? East side of town, duh!"#Witness my brilliant battling!"ZMinerals are great reference material. You wouldn't happen to have, say, an Eviolite?"2It's quite obscure, so...please part with it."@Ahh...spectacular. I hope this battle is just as beautiful!"U...shading like this, coloring like that... sorry, what? Did you need something?"XNo? Well, they're quite rare. Perhaps Nature's Gallery offers them... east of here.".Style and substance are one and the same!"ZCompared to Noel, my fashion is lacking. But with a Ninja Scarf, I'd stand right out!"4Could I gently request one from you... perhaps?"OTo express my gratitude, we shall battle. A chance to show off your style!"OMy reputation lies in tatters. How will I ever live up to Noel's standard?"ZI heard a rumor that they're being sold in Prizca Castle. A man by the name of Diego."!It's time to bring you down!"LHauling sculptures is too hard. It'd be much easier with a Float Stone."Got one on hand?"9Efficient! There'll be time enough for a battle now!"ASorry, but I won't be able to battle if I throw out my back!"fYou don't have one. Well, Nature's Gallery will have them in stock. That's two shops to the east."7I'm skilled in everything. That includes battling!"MYou look ready to help me find a Knight Helmet. Don't ask why I need it."So, cough it up."%My safety comes first. En garde!"EDon't you know who I am? I can't keep risking my head every day!"_Tch, don't have one? They sell them in the castle courtyard. Diego's something or another."L\wm<i>The mention of a certain someone manifests a ball of light...</i>"D\wm<i>You get the sense that you've collected enough light.</i>"0\wm<i>Your friend will be very pleased.</i>"4\wm<i>You should visit her very nice house.</i>"?\wm<i>She is waiting for you <imp>near Velenz</imp>...</i>"Q\wm<i>You get the sense that you've found about half the light you need.</i>"8\wm<i>Your friend is waiting with anticipation.</i>"(\wm<i>Continue your collection.</i>"J\wm<i>A <imp>vision of golden light</imp> appears in your mind...</i>"\wm\ss<i>{1}</i>"+A tattered notebook sits on the table."!It's titled "Tapu Log Book.""Notes: Cruel Cocoon"Notes: Turbulent Sky"Notes: Primal Forest"Notes: Misdirecting Fog"Stop Reading"*Which section would you like to read?"~Tapu Lele's ability "Flutter Totem" creates a "Cruel Cocoon" upon entry that only affects its side and lasts for 6 turns."TAt the end of each turn, it heals Pokemon on its side by 1/8th of their max HP."IHowever, they also lose 1 PP from each of their moves. Cruel indeed."}Tapu Koko's ability "Storm Totem" creates a "Turbulent Sky" upon entry that only affects its side and lasts for 6 turns."�Pokemon on its side get a 30% move damage boost, but they are prevented from using moves that are the same type as the move they most recently used."SOr, to state it another way, they can't use the same move type twice in a row."|Tapu Bulu's ability "Wild Totem" creates a "Primal Forest" upon entry that only affects its side and lasts for 6 turns."VWhenever a Pokemon on its side is hit by an offensive attack, it becomes enraged."jThereby, its defense stats are both lowered by 1 step and its attack stats are both raised by 1 step."~Tapu Fini's ability "Fog Totem" creates a "Misdirecting Fog" upon entry that only affects its side and lasts for 6 turns."mWhenever a foe finishes attacking a Pokemon on its side, the attacker is forced to switch out of battle."wUnlike moves such as Roar or Whirlwind, however, the trainer has enough time to select the replacement themselves."You put down the book."Leave it."Punch it!"Kick it!"Hug it?""A hanging bag. Give it a hit?""You decide to leave it alone."7Your fist makes a satisfying thud against the bag."Oww, you hurt your wrist!"GYou thrust your hips at the right time, and send the
